865fc3da3a947476e368acb141","sha":"cbafed54489188865fc3da3a947476e368acb141","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NathanNeurotic/SeekDeep-DiscordBot/commits/cbafed54489188865fc3da3a947476e368acb141"}],"sha":"130d9c2c1d9b09c120c9ca01389933ec23d0b0e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NathanNeurotic/SeekDeep-DiscordBot/commits/130d9c2c1d9b09c120c9ca01389933ec23d0b0e1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/109461996?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NathanNeurotic","id":109461996,"login":"NathanNeurotic","node_id":"U_kgDOBoZB7A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NathanNeurotic/SeekDeep-DiscordBot/commits/cbafed54489188865fc3da3a947476e368acb141/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-23T02:46:28Z","email":"noahtkevans@gmail.com","name":"NathanNeurotic (Ripto)"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-23T02:46:28Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(gui): logs poll — a bad JSON response no longer floods the viewer with duplicates (v10.38.227) (#269)\n\nGemini on PR #268. The /logs/tail poll did `await r.json().catch(() => null)`:\non an r.ok response whose body fails to parse (truncated/malformed mid-stream),\ndata became null → lines became [] → and it wrote that empty result into the\ndedup cursor (`_prevLogSigs = []`) AND returned true (success). The next good\npoll then saw an empty cursor, treated the whole 200-line window as new, and\nre-appended all of it — a duplication flood.\n\nFix:\n- Drop the `.catch(() => null)` so a parse failure throws to the poll''s own\n  catch, which leaves _prevLogSigs intact and falls back to the calm waiting\n  state (return false → backoff).\n- Belt-and-suspenders: only advance the cursor (and re-arm SSE) when the poll\n  actually returned lines. A valid {ok:false} \"no log file yet\" payload or any\n  empty response no longer clobbers the cursor either. /logs/tail is append-only,\n  so a real log never shrinks to zero — a zero-line poll is always anomalous.\n\nPre-existing latent bug in the original poll viewer, surfaced reviewing the\nboot-calm fix. Swept gui/*.js for the same swallow-to-falsy-then-write-state\npattern; only this poll feeds a persistent cursor, the rest are one-shot reads.\n\nPreflight 8/0, smoke 746/0.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"19f8c00e65bcf917fdb759816604e687a53f6dae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NathanNeurotic/SeekDeep-DiscordBot/git/trees/19f8c00e65bcf917fdb759816604e687a53f6dae"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NathanNeurotic/SeekDeep-DiscordBot/git/commits/cbafed54489188865fc3da3a947476e368acb141","verification":{"payload":"tree 19f8c00e65bcf917fdb759816604e687a53f6dae\nparent a7e8578c6acf850e7e380c46497276a2764d2f1c\nauthor NathanNeurotic (Ripto) <noahtkevans@gmail.com> 1782182788 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782182788 -0700\n\nfix(gui): logs poll — a bad JSON response no longer floods the viewer with duplicates (v10.38.227) (#269)\n\nGemini on PR #268. The /logs/tail poll did `await r.json().catch(() => null)`:\non an r.ok response whose body fails to parse (truncated/malformed mid-stream),\ndata became null → lines became [] → and it wrote that empty result into the\ndedup cursor (`_prevLogSigs = []`) AND returned true (success). The next good\npoll then saw an empty cursor, treated the whole 200-line window as new, and\nre-appended all of it — a duplication flood.\n\nFix:\n- Drop the `.catch(() => null)` so a parse failure throws to the poll''s own\n  catch, which leaves _prevLogSigs intact and falls back to the calm waiting\n  state (return false → backoff).\n- Belt-and-suspenders: only advance the cursor (and re-arm SSE) when the poll\n  actually returned lines. A valid {ok:false} \"no log file yet\" payload or any\n  empty response no longer clobbers the cursor either. /logs/tail is append-only,\n  so a real log never shrinks to zero — a zero-line poll is always anomalous.\n\nPre-existing latent bug in the original poll viewer, surfaced reviewing the\nboot-calm fix. Swept gui/*.js for the same swallow-to-falsy-then-write-state\npattern; only this poll feeds a persistent cursor, the rest are one-shot reads.\n\nPreflight 8/0, smoke 746/0.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOfOECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2uAQAJDsxslphl8UiHTyVBdYMsMT\nGUZq2HPHK3Y3xe2ZFf2kDq+hfSphP1/kSFvGuKXMxkA0VUQmaS9bPc/LjF1lDTG6\npydEKkM/hxzQCeLxK1flncbuoDmFCJ2bk491v9SXWUfGh/oG6quqmbeUQqsiLFnX\n725s4J/pb1EElA2xbwPFM1bNlfZ/uG3T546u+llOHMhWJNcjpxA587avgIMTX/EW\n+LE6mVo+NgFz/OLFkPMSpE7SiB+v2Ulq0YNRmjTg1gEYCZn6IrUXaV62o1qEWddc\nPL1JxJ0fYu2OGvkodtV3fw6IFP5K42UHS3WtONA4MscIprtB6HVlzmYKBtK3SkpT\nfDeiq8UcEfv/QYpORjbIG3A6WZNM78AqjMwpK489W9+16XE/EK1ZDDYBPavjKo0D\nHShT0mbEgG+IVdifaLm2hQSZu0ko2rhkLubq6NrWyuT3wXOf+GVgTi7ysjPtk6mf\n/eW/1O1y6U/cEe6dXirzhiGB+ox9bkOfxbs0oNlaTgcci8awrbKQ2AsAjIykcIV4\nkCMf9wSqJ4nog8RyEIIkBreTqjvS7p9KYu+OJnSPp+dwEUY/WREL6Nwq8ZTVpWja\nDpU0bnnux3aNlbLAzZRYB76lDBtcMYMWWgVSff0iSak3IqDnB6YC/oLSA2M/WjV7\njnIIY92ZCS4a40/Gsw6G\n=1Hw+\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-23T02:46:29Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NathanNeurotic/SeekDeep-DiscordBot/commit/cbafed54489188865fc3da3a947476e368acb141","node_id":"C_kwDOSly7ZdoAKGNiYWZlZDU0NDg5MTg4ODY1ZmMzZGEzYTk0NzQ3NmUzNjhhY2IxNDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NathanNeurotic/SeekDeep-DiscordBot/commit/a7e8578c6acf850e7e380c46497276a2764d2f1c","sha":"a7e8578c6acf850e7e380c46497276a2764d2f1c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NathanNeurotic/SeekDeep-DiscordBot/commits/a7e8578c6acf850e7e380c46497276a2764d2f1c"}],"sha":"cbafed54489188865fc3da3a947476e368acb141","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NathanNeurotic/SeekDeep-DiscordBot/commits/cbafed54489188865fc3da3a947476e368acb141"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/109461996?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NathanNeurotic","id":109461996,"login":"NathanNeurotic","node_id":"U_kgDOBoZB7A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NathanNeurotic/SeekDeep-DiscordBot/commits/a7e8578c6acf850e7e380c46497276a2764d2f1c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-23T02:26:53Z","email":"noahtkevans@gmail.com","name":"NathanNeurotic (Ripto)"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-23T02:26:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(gui): logs viewer — calm boot (no 401 toast) + re-arm SSE after boot race (v10.38.226) (#268)\n\nFixes a regression from the logs-viewer consolidation that made a normal (slow)\nboot look broken — the symptom in the screenshot: a red \"SeekDeep /logs/tail\ninitial · HTTP 401\" toast + a \"logs unavailable\" banner.\n\nRoot cause: the consolidated viewer fires its initial /logs/tail fetch and opens\nSSE the instant the page loads. During a cold boot the AI server isn''t up yet,\nso the GUI auth token can''t be fetched and the request 401s. loadInitial treated\nthat transient boot race as a hard failure: it threw, which routed to\nSeekDeepDebug.warn (toasts non-timeout errors) AND painted a red \"logs\nunavailable\" banner. (The old app.page2 viewer dodged this by only loading when\nyou opened the Logs pane, by which point the token was ready.)\n\nFixes:\n- loadInitial + pollOnce now fail CALMLY on the boot 401: no toast (console.warn\n  only), and a muted \"▸ waiting for the server…\" placeholder instead of a red\n  error. The boot-sequence panel + POLL/OFFLINE pill already explain the state.\n  The poll loop quietly retries and renders the backlog once the server answers.\n- Second regression fixed: once SSE hit the boot 401 it gave up permanently (a\n  fatal status isn''t retried), leaving you stuck in 3s polling after boot instead\n  of live streaming. pollOnce now re-arms SSE (`if (!sse) startSSE()`) the moment\n  the server is reachable again, upgrading back to live /logs/stream. Added an\n  _sseStarting guard so the poll-driven re-arm can''t open a duplicate EventSource.\n- startSSE / poll catch paths use console.warn instead of the toasting\n  SeekDeepDebug.warn (a failed background poll shouldn''t toast).\n\nThe boot time itself is the AI server loading models into VRAM (unchanged); this\njust stops the GUI from looking broken while it loads.\n\nPreflight 8/0, smoke 746/0.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ff281a9b11a364ee8823d4cf009ba128fdffd896","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NathanNeurotic/SeekDeep-DiscordBot/git/trees/ff281a9b11a364ee8823d4cf009ba128fdffd896"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NathanNeurotic/SeekDeep-DiscordBot/git/commits/a7e8578c6acf850e7e380c46497276a2764d2f1c","verification":{"payload":"tree ff281a9b11a364ee8823d4cf009ba128fdffd896\nparent 5556b50c32320d08c79c7206420d82e4710a6482\nauthor NathanNeurotic (Ripto) <noahtkevans@gmail.com> 1782181613 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782181613 -0700\n\nfix(gui): logs viewer — calm boot (no 401 toast) + re-arm SSE after boot race (v10.38.226) (#268)\n\nFixes a regression from the logs-viewer consolidation that made a normal (slow)\nboot look broken — the symptom in the screenshot: a red \"SeekDeep /logs/tail\ninitial · HTTP 401\" toast + a \"logs unavailable\" banner.\n\nRoot cause: the consolidated viewer fires its initial /logs/tail fetch and opens\nSSE the instant the page loads. During a cold boot the AI server isn''t up yet,\nso the GUI auth token can''t be fetched and the request 401s. loadInitial treated\nthat transient boot race as a hard failure: it threw, which routed to\nSeekDeepDebug.warn (toasts non-timeout errors) AND painted a red \"logs\nunavailable\" banner. (The old app.page2 viewer dodged this by only loading when\nyou opened the Logs pane, by which point the token was ready.)\n\nFixes:\n- loadInitial + pollOnce now fail CALMLY on the boot 401: no toast (console.warn\n  only), and a muted \"▸ waiting for the server…\" placeholder instead of a red\n  error. The boot-sequence panel + POLL/OFFLINE pill already explain the state.\n  The poll loop quietly retries and renders the backlog once the server answers.\n- Second regression fixed: once SSE hit the boot 401 it gave up permanently (a\n  fatal status isn''t retried), leaving you stuck in 3s polling after boot instead\n  of live streaming. pollOnce now re-arms SSE (`if (!sse) startSSE()`) the moment\n  the server is reachable again, upgrading back to live /logs/stream. Added an\n  _sseStarting guard so the poll-driven re-arm can''t open a duplicate EventSource.\n- startSSE / poll catch paths use console.warn instead of the toasting\n  SeekDeepDebug.warn (a failed background poll shouldn''t toast).\n\nThe boot time itself is the AI server loading models into VRAM (unchanged); this\njust stops the GUI from looking broken while it loads.\n\nPreflight 8/0, smoke 746/0.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOe7tCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAUAQQADfekvTTuJ47vEl+Htu08DtG\nwqdJ6obv1G/cJgRSo4ARDTiRXNykDbfGHfs4pFHtFwKgZIwyIXaHK4vQTmBtWQzl\n63pbV0Uusw3vmPsTRu+zpPX/zzkw/cFbHvjJWhjp7KOEaEcfim/mZaco+qX5XLe9\nBSBmkvn2uZa9SNentYYbT/5kswChbkE4XWZOIXnAyoPNEX8DVix+LwRfVT7E7L0Y\ngPAjElgTBaITpeXy3yrOtdHiKSJnebcrGrGObK1AHes8b2+2yvujdHV8xc2Pkshm\nzkDq7xnRMoMNOGD+GSCrs69AzgUWd