om/repos/NathanNeurotic/SeekDeep-DiscordBot/commits/a7e8578c6acf850e7e380c46497276a2764d2f1c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/109461996?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NathanNeurotic","id":109461996,"login":"NathanNeurotic","node_id":"U_kgDOBoZB7A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NathanNeurotic/SeekDeep-DiscordBot/commits/5556b50c32320d08c79c7206420d82e4710a6482/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-23T01:54:13Z","email":"noahtkevans@gmail.com","name":"NathanNeurotic (Ripto)"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-23T01:54:13Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(gui): Gemini follow-ups on the logs-consolidation + #264 PRs — 3 GUI fixes (v10.38.225) (#267)\n\n1. app.page5.js — keep SSE''s native auto-reconnect. The consolidated logs\n   viewer force-closed the EventSource and nulled it on any error, which DISABLES\n   the browser''s built-in reconnect: a transient blip (server restart mid-stream)\n   permanently downgraded the pane to 3s polling until reload/pause-resume. Now we\n   flip the pill to POLL on error and let EventSource reconnect itself (onopen\n   restores LIVE; the poll loop covers the gap). We only release the handle when\n   it has truly given up (readyState === CLOSED — a fatal HTTP status the browser\n   won''t retry anyway), so a later pause->resume can still re-open it.\n\n2. app.page5.js — a failed initial /logs/tail load no longer leaves the pane\n   blank. It now renders a \"logs unavailable · <reason>\" line (like the old\n   app.page2 viewer), via textContent so the error string can''t inject markup;\n   it self-clears the moment SSE or a later poll delivers a line (lineCount===0).\n\n3. app.page2.js — null-guard the \"both\"-mode restore. The v10.38.224 clobber\n   fix compared the active chip to the raw chip we set; with no raw chip to set\n   that was a null===null false-match. Guarded with `rawChip &&` so we only\n   restore when there was genuinely a selection of ours to revert.\n\nPreflight 8/0, smoke 746/0.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fd5c9e20cd82f293fb9682edb193bbd4187195a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NathanNeurotic/SeekDeep-DiscordBot/git/trees/fd5c9e20cd82f293fb9682edb193bbd4187195a8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NathanNeurotic/SeekDeep-DiscordBot/git/commits/5556b50c32320d08c79c7206420d82e4710a6482","verification":{"payload":"tree fd5c9e20cd82f293fb9682edb193bbd4187195a8\nparent 11eb970983d42e0cc887d7e3ef3aa70eac0987d6\nauthor NathanNeurotic (Ripto) <noahtkevans@gmail.com> 1782179653 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782179653 -0700\n\nfix(gui): Gemini follow-ups on the logs-consolidation + #264 PRs — 3 GUI fixes (v10.38.225) (#267)\n\n1. app.page5.js — keep SSE''s native auto-reconnect. The consolidated logs\n   viewer force-closed the EventSource and nulled it on any error, which DISABLES\n   the browser''s built-in reconnect: a transient blip (server restart mid-stream)\n   permanently downgraded the pane to 3s polling until reload/pause-resume. Now we\n   flip the pill to POLL on error and let EventSource reconnect itself (onopen\n   restores LIVE; the poll loop covers the gap). We only release the handle when\n   it has truly given up (readyState === CLOSED — a fatal HTTP status the browser\n   won''t retry anyway), so a later pause->resume can still re-open it.\n\n2. app.page5.js — a failed initial /logs/tail load no longer leaves the pane\n   blank. It now renders a \"logs unavailable · <reason>\" line (like the old\n   app.page2 viewer), via textContent so the error string can''t inject markup;\n   it self-clears the moment SSE or a later poll delivers a line (lineCount===0).\n\n3. app.page2.js — null-guard the \"both\"-mode restore. The v10.38.224 clobber\n   fix compared the active chip to the raw chip we set; with no raw chip to set\n   that was a null===null false-match. Guarded with `rawChip &&` so we only\n   restore when there was genuinely a selection of ours to revert.\n\nPreflight 8/0, smoke 746/0.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOedFCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAlrkQAC1rJY6v0Z+Ww253tZ1XL70x\nepy6ObrEbRYvjPhTg6l7ApBfwdqQjWVV9jAsgIUtU3e7heRynj7ioc0doHPZO0i5\nmYnGtzeomWWCEKblZWL64Nxdc/7+r9FgrBAF7v+0bKW/jZjZdTBqchQY0sLiw1Ic\nSmcSAjnewultS9D0VDM/YXM5/fwg5F165EqsFcBhFFVAb8RwPnZDQ+aKsn3neTKl\nZ8rNmEXiDNz3bJCKeVsh+G530REiy6EEQ9Nk2pmlpzmj4QxQXCP1oD+F2+Fi0jBh\n2emhDF+IJZP2sl8XEkFxA9jz8F/nAK3bU3oG00zqNEyhQeizZXd9ZES4168YlxQd\n52nAPNZNE4MPcxkGmOEcQcZB7C/QiW1xLstOPJJmWBSjkgMn7FaZ5FGeNHFr7+3N\noV0ehCk255kD+7sycrO5+djMlmgMz9aWanNa0hdCNYEOxLrlm2N4usALMvQsSxai\nLptXNXkgR5lZ2Owk3CRGHNK83XcLdn1YmsSlngLo+GCNUEkBhNISGCxzxUjxGiA9\nX5hBW7O68gQBl22ZLBjbb02gFjDPTJlRilsULdlEhBVk4kHp2d2kQJBUj05Kulyb\nOstNM5D2Q5Zo+Irj3BGQKZYy2yFgRmErQgsXFSa4+Mq/Pl/LSBJzP/vFkqWw/Qi3\nvHI4gdFx3zKdds0hRt5w\n=R8R4\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-23T01:54:13Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NathanNeurotic/SeekDeep-DiscordBot/commit/5556b50c32320d08c79c7206420d82e4710a6482","node_id":"C_kwDOSly7ZdoAKDU1NTZiNTBjMzIzMjBkMDhjNzljNzIwNjQyMGQ4MmU0NzEwYTY0ODI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NathanNeurotic/SeekDeep-DiscordBot/commit/11eb970983d42e0cc887d7e3ef3aa70eac0987d6","sha":"11eb970983d42e0cc887d7e3ef3aa70eac0987d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NathanNeurotic/SeekDeep-DiscordBot/commits/11eb970983d42e0cc887d7e3ef3aa70eac0987d6"}],"sha":"5556b50c32320d08c79c7206420d82e4710a6482","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NathanNeurotic/SeekDeep-DiscordBot/commits/5556b50c32320d08c79c7206420d82e4710a6482"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/109461996?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NathanNeurotic","id":109461996,"login":"NathanNeurotic","node_id":"U_kgDOBoZB7A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NathanNeurotic/SeekDeep-DiscordBot/commits/11eb970983d42e0cc887d7e3ef3aa70eac0987d6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-23T00:35:52Z","email":"noahtkevans@gmail.com","name":"NathanNeurotic (Ripto)"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-23T00:35:52Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(gui): Gemini PR #264 follow-ups — both-mode chip race + updater skip-listener leak (v10.38.224) (#266)\n\nTwo GUI fixes from Gemini''s review of PR #264, each confirmed against the live\ncode by an independent verify pass. A completeness sweep of the rest of gui/*.js\nfor the same two bug classes found NO other real instances (the model-install\nswap popover, notify.js Escape handler, emoji-vault/bot-bridge finally blocks,\nand ~20 button-label restores are all already self-cleaning or guarded).\n\n1. app.page2.js — image A/B \"both\" mode could clobber a manual chip change.\n   The deferred raw pass flips the refine chip to `raw` and its .finally()\n   restored the prior selection unconditionally on settle. If the user clicked a\n   different refine chip while that second pass was still generating (several\n   seconds), their choice was silently reverted. Now restores only if the chip we\n   set (raw) is still the active one — a manual mid-pass change is left alone.\n   Also dropped the redundant Promise.resolve() around the already-async\n   generate() (verified: generate is `async`, can''t throw synchronously, so\n   rejection handling is unchanged).\n\n2. updater.js — \"skip this version\" document click-listener no longer leaks.\n   skipHandler only detached itself on the skip path; dismissing the banner any\n   other way (the X, \"Remind me later\", \"View release\") left it bound to document\n   for the page''s life. It now self-cleans on the next click once the banner is\n   gone. (Registered after the banner is in the DOM, so it can''t detach early\n   while the banner is still showing.)\n\nPreflight 8/0, smoke 746/0.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"40af7411bb29398b292552ff7a1781f9225cc5c5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NathanNeurotic/SeekDeep-DiscordBot/git/trees/40af7411bb29398b292552ff7a1781f9225cc5c5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NathanNeurotic/SeekDeep-DiscordBot/git/commits/11eb970983d42e0cc887d7e3ef3aa70eac0987d6","verification":{"payload":"tree 40af7411bb29398b292552ff7a1781f9225cc5c5\nparent 7d29d54afaf2696ede4387c5485f2fde431a0811\nauthor NathanNeurotic (Ripto) <noahtkevans@gmail.com> 1782174952 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782174952 -0700\n\nfix(gui): Gemini PR #264 follow-ups — both-mode chip race + updater skip-listener leak (v10.38.224) (#266)\n\nTwo GUI fixes from Gemini''s review of PR #264, each confirmed against the live\ncode by an independent verify pass. A completeness sweep of the rest of gui/*.js\nfor the same two bug classes found NO other real instances (the model-install\nswap popover, notify.js Escape handler, emoji-vault/bot-bridge finally blocks,\nand ~20 button-label restores are all already self-cleaning or guarded).\n\n1. app.page2.js — image A/B \"both\" mode could clobber a manual chip change.\n   The deferred raw pass flips the refine chip to `raw` and its .finally()\n   restored the prior selection unconditionally on settle. If the user clicked a\n   different refine chip while that second pass was still generating (several\n   seconds), their choice was silently reverted. Now restores only if the chip we\n   set (raw) is still the active one — a manual mid-pass change is left alone.\n   Also dropped the redundant Promise.resolve() around the already-async\n   generate() (verified: generate is `async`, can''t throw synchronously, so\n   rejection handling is unchanged).\n\n2. updater.js — \"skip this version\" document click-listener no longer leaks.\n   skipHandler only detached itself on the skip path; dismissing the banner any\n   other way (the X, \"Remind me later\", \"View release\") left it bound to document\n   for the page''s life. It now self-cleans on the next click once the banner is\n   gone. (Registered after the banner is in the DOM, so it can''t detach early\n   while the banner is still showing.)\n\nPreflight 8/0, smoke 746/0.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOdToCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA0fcQAAZYNpjxSVy2okkT0c0kHL14\nObKa3VYUtaXw4bXjraxORLl9b3xHKJhUrOkwu2RIcZPbTJVdhq2orXbzTr4L+uZj\nRS0I2ooiULZOZDG+94Ge3GH4XKDGlH+ZPTF//WaX85T8j58GwPd8HQTbtlO9sUxB\nxxLRmQADl9OPOFDg8tNTlYXhyiJLisuqgP8dnJ/GgtApwItVP4cc+FYyuY/UVR3f\nVIrRk3f6BmEnIFKecUHnyKPaRnQuTzEG3CaKQ4Wb6zQ+8rboqDiPMRyaFJB7AahZ\nRKgD4GtENFExxXnm98SLLGvEQOopVATmN1W3PhiamTQ7fGcHRM9ZTC40t58noBoi\nXhdu2tJqGefUJd1gXusT/DfdUzuq0zA/Iso92lewgGGsEAt1uknPRvo3aA7KyyG+\n16fgk8voA4OrJIX2J9twSOkoxHjXRwuezKyXAEdFQOfgE8WbOO2T5H+989/8iKET\nQqzKgXbcTVFYuPZAmsaatfkzeRizlNXxEyQuWomlonM5ysllirEvze8P8s7qoTm8\n+mFelwTNikrK4v5DEJAOxUeKwK37ixdzA5kPNhOpsTxat/FYtEbCV8XMPyVHsfaR\nL4eSVHSUWH1kvvPwbEpsntl8oCzmOM/46NSWpJiAjY19f8//2/H2Wb/v0b47BbuA\nx4nyo4GiR/YUV5JPvcS9\n=ett7\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-23T00:35:53Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NathanNeurotic/SeekDeep-DiscordBot/commit/11eb970983d42e0cc887d7e3ef3aa70eac0987d6","node_id":"C_kwDOSly7ZdoAKDExZWI5NzA5ODNkNDJlMGNjODg3ZDdlM2VmM2FhNzBlYWMwOTg3ZDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NathanNeurotic/SeekDeep-DiscordBot/commit/7d29d54afaf2696ede4387c5485f2fde431a0811","sha":"7d29d54afaf2696ede4387c5485f2fde431a0811","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NathanNeurotic/SeekDeep-DiscordBot/commits/7d29d54afaf2696ede4387c5485f2fde431a0811"}],"sha":"11eb970983d42e0cc887d7e3ef3aa70eac0987d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NathanNeurotic/SeekDeep-DiscordBot/commits/11eb970983d42e0cc887d7e3ef3aa70eac0987d6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/109461996?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NathanNeurotic","id":109461996,"login":"NathanNeurotic","node_id":"U_kgDOBoZB7A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NathanNeurotic/SeekDeep-DiscordBot/commits/7d29d54afaf2696ede4387c5485f2fde431a0811/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-23T00:18:00Z","email":"noahtkevans@gmail.com","name":"NathanNeurotic (Ripto)"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-23T00:18:00Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(gui): consolidate the Logs pane into one viewer — SSE + poll fallback + filters + header (v10.38.223) (#265)\n\nThe Control Center Logs pane was wired by TWO independent viewers at once:\napp.page2.js (SSE /logs/stream + level/source/search filters + file/size header)\nand app.page5.js (/logs/tail poll fallback + dedup cursor + LIVE/POLL mode pill).\nBoth targeted #logs-wrap, so every line rendered twice (in two different row\nstyles) and Pause/Clear fired two handlers. This was the 4th item deferred from\naudit batch 3b, held for a live test because neither viewer was a clean superset\nof the other — deleting either dropped real features.\n\nMerged into a single owner in app.page5.js:\n- keeps page5''s dedup cursor, LIVE/POLL mode pill, and /logs/tail poll fallback\n- gains page2''s level/source/search filters, header truth-up, and SSE streaming\n  (rows now carry data-level/data-src so the filters work on page5''s renderer)\n- live path is now SSE /logs/stream, which seeks to EOF and tails the active log\n  FILE directly, so it streams live WITHOUT SEEKDEEP_EMIT_LOG_LINES (the old\n  WS-bus path required that flag and otherwise sat in poll mode); poll takes over\n  transparently if SSE drops\n- a shared parseLogLine() normalizes the raw string lines from BOTH /logs/tail\n  and SSE (file-logger + legacy formats), so levels/timestamps render correctly\n- removed the duplicate wireLogsViewer from app.page2.js (211 lines)\n\nRegenerated docs/ENDPOINT_COVERAGE.md (/logs/stream now attributed to page5).\nPreflight 8/0, smoke 746/0.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2d688ac56bd59a0c75d56207ae916d1fdd2160bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NathanNeurotic/SeekDeep-DiscordBot/git/trees/2d688ac56bd59a0c75d56207ae916d1fdd2160bb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NathanNeurotic/SeekDeep-DiscordBot/git/commits/7d29d54afaf2696ede4387c5485f2fde431a0811","verification":{"payload":"tree 2d688ac56bd59a0c75d56207ae916d1fdd2160bb\nparent 368a7a3630cdd438d8de6ee7d0b2b7ebad3e7a1b\nauthor NathanNeurotic (Ripto) <noahtkevans@gmail.com> 1782173880 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782173880 -0700\n\nfix(gui): consolidate the Logs pane into one viewer — SSE + poll fallback + filters + header (v10.38.223) (#265)\n\nThe Control Center Logs pane was wired by TWO independent viewers at once:\napp.page2.js (SSE /logs/stream + level/source/search filters + file/size header)\nand app.page5.js (/logs/tail poll fallback + dedup cursor + LIVE/POLL mode pill).\nBoth targeted #logs-wrap, so every line rendered twice (in two different row\nstyles) and Pause/Clear fired two handlers. This was the 4th item deferred from\naudit batch 3b, held for a live test because neither viewer was a clean superset\nof the other — deleting either dropped real features.\n\nMerged into a single owner in app.page5.js:\n- keeps page5''s dedup cursor, LIVE/POLL mode pill, and /logs/tail poll fallback\n- gains page2''s level/source/search filters, header truth-up, and SSE streaming\n  (rows now carry data-level/data-src so the filters work on page5''s renderer)\n- live path is now SSE /logs/stream, which seeks to EOF and tails the active log\n  FILE directly, so it streams live WITHOUT SEEKDEEP_EMIT_LOG_LINES (the old\n  WS-bus path required that flag and otherwise sat in poll mode); poll takes over\n  transparently if SSE drops\n- a shared parseLogLine() normalizes the raw string lines from BOTH /logs/tail\n  and SSE (file-logger + legacy formats), so levels/timestamps render correctly\n- removed the duplicate wireLogsViewer from app.page2.js (211 lines)\n\nRegenerated docs/ENDPOINT_COVERAGE.md (/logs/stream now attributed to page5).\nPreflight 8/0, smoke 746/0.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOdC4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAct4QAJzlZeGCr4OzaJ31xivNDwsS\nwaXFYzRfMtY6pILFjYM7gxdL3aB7cUoUrhr5QNPw2f5elLeREmd5DBs0ZGLTHFWT\nCypIi6fWBLCy1Bt1IBaEVxPcVRKJcxII1oAdMFPmYhSYFp800GiKDIhwHeAmGgyo\nJpIUfsypqzqKEZVBp1sQ8uNe5RKU+8+a9sJCDIM7tH2RURPXJCf43TxxG/WzBL4r\nLBjfITubfpo5d/R4yypkjyc80bvRvXLQbYk/Ryl0ARQiwV7NJnlmI3taucc1J3BJ\nO9YaMci2JGZDYMLcmk4UWvU6mGq/tVIio3ncvXStaJDIt0yW+vj6/S7AO3Dir13n\nDQxped5gcNg1kj61HB3qogRQUBuCknTJannESv3acIha0uJbFg+0Ar2Tbk9TluGn\nkj0M1go3ZviREcxiqJIVEi1GM1cuTSt79Dhko3rb49p24VH4bBkUUA6aRFjpZPh4\nK6qWUH+9QwGIXOePd4uD0XaJwo0X6Rv4w/TTx2amVlN/w0gRtVx4J02v3LqBZv0M\nJVyI4AjqvsZ62QJwm8cF9XSPY3kgDYs/dyKtOD0hcBtehDe41Es7QS/nTpOOmrxM\nfNPXHUksttqD5uCr+ADNvKPPx7Zhb66pK2KvRzNQz8hEqP/c9ku3mmy4L9p74PIh\n/QwiPRdpiJMd4m2TJnxS\n=5ksL\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-23T00:18:00Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NathanNeurotic/SeekDeep-DiscordBot/commit/7d29d54afaf2696ede4387c5485f2fde431a0811","node_id":"C_kwDOSly7ZdoAKDdkMjlkNTRhZmFmMjY5NmVkZTQzODdjNTQ4NWYyZmRlNDMxYTA4MTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NathanNeurotic/SeekDeep-DiscordBot/commit/368a7a3630cdd438d8de6ee7d0b2b7ebad3e7a1b","sha":"368a7a3630cdd438d8de6ee7d0b2b7ebad3e7a1b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NathanNeurotic/SeekDeep-DiscordBot/commits/368a7a3630cdd438d8de6ee7d0b2b7ebad3e7a1b"}],"sha":"7d29d54afaf2696ede4387c5485f2fde431a0811","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NathanNeurotic/SeekDeep-DiscordBot/commits/7d29d54afaf2696ede4387c5485f2fde431a0811"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/109461996?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NathanNeurotic","id":109461996,"login":"NathanNeurotic","node_id":"U_kgDOBoZB7A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NathanNeurotic/SeekDeep-DiscordBot/commits/368a7a3630cdd438d8de6ee7d0b2b7ebad3e7a1b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-22T23:00:24Z","email":"noahtkevans@gmail.com","name":"NathanNeurotic (Ripto)"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-22T23:00:24Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(gui): audit batch 3b — 3 deferred Control Center fixes (v10.38.222) (#264)\n\n(1) \"Stop all\" could START a stopped service. The header Stop-all/Launch-all\nbuttons were double-wired: correctly in launcher.js (POSTs explicit start/stop\nper service by label) AND buggily in app.page2.js, which clicked each card''s\n`.ctl button:last-child` — the STATE-DEPENDENT Stop/Start toggle, so on a\ndown service that button is \"Start\". Removed app.page2.js''s positional\nduplicate; launcher.js is the sole correct owner.\n\n(2) Image \"both\" A/B mode silently behaved like \"refined\". The raw second pass\nwas an inline `await generate(true)` run while inflightCtl was still set (cleared\nonly in the outer finally), so it tripped the in-flight recursion guard, aborted\nthe just-settled controller, and returned without generating. Defer the raw pass\nvia setTimeout(0) so it runs AFTER the finally clears inflightCtl.\n\n(3) Updater \"skip this version\" was unreachable — it lived in a follow-on toast\ngated on the banner being already-closed within 200ms (impossible for a banner\nwith no auto-dismiss). Moved the skip to a link in the update banner body\n(banner() has no tertiary action slot); preserved the SKIP_KEY write + closes\nthe banner on skip.\n\nDeferred (item 4 of the set): the dual-wired Logs pane (app.page2 SSE viewer vs\napp.page5 WS-bus viewer) — removing one needs a live test since it swaps the\nlive-streaming mechanism; the failure mode (broken live logs) outweighs the\ncurrent double-render annoyance.\n\nSmoke 746/0; preflight 8/0.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d075f99e7b65044a3622cc95d5534e778feefa71","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NathanNeurotic/SeekDeep-DiscordBot/git/trees/d075f99e7b65044a3622cc95d5534e778feefa71"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NathanNeurotic/SeekDeep-DiscordBot/git/commits/368a7a3630cdd438d8de6ee7d0b2b7ebad3e7a1b","verification":{"payload":"tree d075f99e7b65044a3622cc95d5534e778feefa71\nparent 03eaea13c5d68f2e4aa42044dc7e16e9e0040898\nauthor NathanNeurotic (Ripto) <noahtkevans@gmail.com> 1782169224 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782169224 -0700\n\nfix(gui): audit batch 3b — 3 deferred Control Center fixes (v10.38.222) (#264)\n\n(1) \"Stop all\" could START a stopped service. The header Stop-all/Launch-all\nbuttons were double-wired: correctly in launcher.js (POSTs explicit start/stop\nper service by label) AND buggily in app.page2.js, which clicked each card''s\n`.ctl button:last-child` — the STATE-DEPENDENT Stop/Start toggle, so on a\ndown service that button is \"Start\". Removed app.page2.js''s positional\nduplicate; launcher.js is the sole correct owner.\n\n(2) Image \"both\" A/B mode silently behaved like \"refined\". The raw second pass\nwas an inline `await generate(true)` run while inflightCtl was still set (cleared\nonly in the outer finally), so it tripped the in-flight recursion guard, aborted\nthe just-settled controller, and returned without generating. Defer the raw pass\nvia setTimeout(0) so it runs AFTER the finally clears inflightCtl.\n\n(3) Updater \"skip this version\" was unreachable — it lived in a follow-on toast\ngated on the banner being already-closed within 200ms (impossible for a banner\nwith no auto-dismiss). Moved the skip to a link in the update banner body\n(banner() has no tertiary action slot); preserved the SKIP_KEY write + closes\nthe banner on skip.\n\nDeferred (item 4 of the set): the dual-wired Logs pane (app.page2 SSE viewer vs\napp.page5 WS-bus viewer) — removing one needs a live test since it swaps the\nlive-streaming mechanism; the failure mode (broken live logs) outweighs the\ncurrent double-render annoyance.\n\nSmoke 746/0; preflight 8/0.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOb6ICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAArdEQAI+iMKCJeT61Ffvm/ObqPKvg\nbrD45zxyQRu+JQp0uFQwf2X0LtseXG4iBHRY+0VIG98ZO7hIG0loteKeSaZWAEep\nC6HSEYZnEs3aBvO05ivu3FmwC6t+F2kXunFJne3MnuEw8prWn9mb1HC/Y9630vHY\n/wyKbQiX8b8pL5/XudpkYv8ted/g6XkmWPieu9k2EFHL1QYu5Rn6tdNJ6A9MAPYV\nBsOM4o8kIIpCqkGXHW6ktK8Atg8tE2vL7dobhtjfpniEm9YxI+SuPnwnwAPzf0Fh\n5H2CcBuol+0MD/ZvnH1t2aTaE4o/TeEbZLl2kWKW0RqwjewSFzmbG01LPGyNCQA0\nbSQirJZINY7HUGpNGcxDsz1/wGF5558Wq2wDoY0/ZP9E+iFXUi6qpEkxaYibEcbF\nEXTXtM8lIAkfkHY/M6HCaPGkhprTAjRW+bAFqwbgrbYHU5oOZs6jEA9HC+aQ7ufm\nTNZo+mDQk1eI7vDc/yySHUwCKW9kXV/qBMxo8HzyJsOHx7FKuwDtKHB80RFgsC7Q\nNvjzlv1qHFBJpHwWysmrFKlUkFzMV9ASt7ygM/E/NLmMSYeXhDl5esHqGanNaxHW\nZ7hwdHg7t/yWfccVKBEXst699ZIk4BOmLNyZcn+CmqnoZxJhCItNDq8uPUGiBvZK\nT1z+MOHCObqu96OubVk4\n=w9/5\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-22T23:00:24Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":