nts":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NathanNeurotic/SeekDeep-DiscordBot/commit/edbef33d3fa0e46108cab247216bf40c89142a74","sha":"edbef33d3fa0e46108cab247216bf40c89142a74","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NathanNeurotic/SeekDeep-DiscordBot/commits/edbef33d3fa0e46108cab247216bf40c89142a74"}],"sha":"0ff0a5c5e123069934244c89a48ce00e94390d55","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NathanNeurotic/SeekDeep-DiscordBot/commits/0ff0a5c5e123069934244c89a48ce00e94390d55"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/109461996?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NathanNeurotic","id":109461996,"login":"NathanNeurotic","node_id":"U_kgDOBoZB7A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NathanNeurotic/SeekDeep-DiscordBot/commits/edbef33d3fa0e46108cab247216bf40c89142a74/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-22T07:52:16Z","email":"noahtkevans@gmail.com","name":"NathanNeurotic (Ripto)"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-22T07:52:16Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: Gemini review follow-ups on the audit batches PRs #243-#248 (v10.38.207) (#249)\n\nNine verified fixes from review of the recent low/nit PRs; one is a real\nregression a prior fix introduced.\n\nServer (gui_endpoints.py):\n- emoji-vault: the \"requests not installed\" 503 I added was swallowed by the\n  surrounding broad `except` in two write paths — bulk import reported it\n  per-emoji as a `network: ...` failure (and returned 200 OK); single-delete\n  flattened it to a misleading 502. Both now `except HTTPException: raise`\n  before the generic catch so the real status surfaces. (real regression)\n- Discord-error message parse guards a non-dict JSON body (isinstance).\n- newest-log picker uses max() instead of a full sort.\n\nServer (local_ai_server.py):\n- _output_path once/60s prune now uses double-checked locking (_PRUNE_LOCK):\n  concurrent threadpool requests could both prune and churn I/O / hit OSError.\n- live TTS-voice swap drops the cached engine UNDER _TTS_ENGINE_LOCK; an\n  unlocked reset could be clobbered by a concurrent first-call /tts finishing\n  a build of the OLD voice (stale handle vs the env we just rewrote).\n\nGUI:\n- stats breakdown shows a styled \"No <persona/style/model> activity recorded\n  yet\" placeholder (uses the previously-unused label param) instead of a blank\n  gap when counts drop to zero.\n- ctx-menu error logger is typeof-guarded (a non-function SeekDeepDebug.warn\n  could have thrown).\n- Safe-mode/hidden-tab poll-skip check centralized into one shared\n  window.seekdeepSkipBgPoll() in nav.js (was re-derived in five places:\n  app.page1/2/5.js + launcher.js).\n- Model Manager legend: added the missing UNLOADED pill (the common default\n  state). Kept CACHED (set on model-evict by app.page5.js) and NOT INSTALLED\n  (set on uninstall by app.page4.js) — Gemini flagged them as never-rendered,\n  but they ARE rendered, just by other code paths into the same cell.\n\nRejected (PR #244): offloading the _REQ_LOCK acquisition off the event loop in\nthe request-metrics middleware — the lock is held by threadpool threads for a\ncounter bump only (nanoseconds, uncontended); the \"fix\" adds overhead for no\nmeasurable benefit. Gemini itself rated the impact small.\n\nPreflight 8/0; gui-smoke 279/0 (main venv).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"616d58db3b4c3459ce7b7e315237ef453ae3886c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NathanNeurotic/SeekDeep-DiscordBot/git/trees/616d58db3b4c3459ce7b7e315237ef453ae3886c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NathanNeurotic/SeekDeep-DiscordBot/git/commits/edbef33d3fa0e46108cab247216bf40c89142a74","verification":{"payload":"tree 616d58db3b4c3459ce7b7e315237ef453ae3886c\nparent b7c290bd4425100db44b47400eec1540b573de72\nauthor NathanNeurotic (Ripto) <noahtkevans@gmail.com> 1782114736 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782114736 -0700\n\nfix: Gemini review follow-ups on the audit batches PRs #243-#248 (v10.38.207) (#249)\n\nNine verified fixes from review of the recent low/nit PRs; one is a real\nregression a prior fix introduced.\n\nServer (gui_endpoints.py):\n- emoji-vault: the \"requests not installed\" 503 I added was swallowed by the\n  surrounding broad `except` in two write paths — bulk import reported it\n  per-emoji as a `network: ...` failure (and returned 200 OK); single-delete\n  flattened it to a misleading 502. Both now `except HTTPException: raise`\n  before the generic catch so the real status surfaces. (real regression)\n- Discord-error message parse guards a non-dict JSON body (isinstance).\n- newest-log picker uses max() instead of a full sort.\n\nServer (local_ai_server.py):\n- _output_path once/60s prune now uses double-checked locking (_PRUNE_LOCK):\n  concurrent threadpool requests could both prune and churn I/O / hit OSError.\n- live TTS-voice swap drops the cached engine UNDER _TTS_ENGINE_LOCK; an\n  unlocked reset could be clobbered by a concurrent first-call /tts finishing\n  a build of the OLD voice (stale handle vs the env we just rewrote).\n\nGUI:\n- stats breakdown shows a styled \"No <persona/style/model> activity recorded\n  yet\" placeholder (uses the previously-unused label param) instead of a blank\n  gap when counts drop to zero.\n- ctx-menu error logger is typeof-guarded (a non-function SeekDeepDebug.warn\n  could have thrown).\n- Safe-mode/hidden-tab poll-skip check centralized into one shared\n  window.seekdeepSkipBgPoll() in nav.js (was re-derived in five places:\n  app.page1/2/5.js + launcher.js).\n- Model Manager legend: added the missing UNLOADED pill (the common default\n  state). Kept CACHED (set on model-evict by app.page5.js) and NOT INSTALLED\n  (set on uninstall by app.page4.js) — Gemini flagged them as never-rendered,\n  but they ARE rendered, just by other code paths into the same cell.\n\nRejected (PR #244): offloading the _REQ_LOCK acquisition off the event loop in\nthe request-metrics middleware — the lock is held by threadpool threads for a\ncounter bump only (nanoseconds, uncontended); the \"fix\" adds overhead for no\nmeasurable benefit. Gemini itself rated the impact small.\n\nPreflight 8/0; gui-smoke 279/0 (main venv).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOOmwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATQ4QAEH4rdB6IaEDXbJZrCV7hftV\ntqV65IWL0o1tIdathF78CaezF0PKo9Hvyk8bkVeEWys9xFUKjnoBzTEGrege4GAL\nrNiHobUQoXtigBRCLlFTo4ISy+utBPkQfXf0yJqe05fUhs9YLcKFaGs7rxRZbigq\n67zaw96eFL4s/SOsiORxwglOTDDcXQhvdFQep3vjx49xY3FFAWVY85E0692wgoFL\nPOMDNrgVJbTCwK3jUqX+vhsBw7/FjMqjpZ4vM2wHLct9j5C3HD02kMVYXbZv4FqV\nMunfynUkmJkM2DGc8gwX9rEMM5cIsecyOTobDuyA+Bhlid1r3VeXLunknWDxycT4\ncHURvjN+uqW2NmnO0Hppgf9+OpKInEOQUtwNTk7I1uggcqI/XFL9Z8+AOHZvqtBu\nLTp2tJsAtFOOWPxC1zThd9b321iL4FYSbIi0DrhtSyyJC/dHEST+RSRHppsLz9hN\nf47GKqs4071UMX+hiVrM7XpDFWkOE7DwLIStS+TR/At2l635ouXcsPyaUrAl3vqV\nR5rDEa5MOlKhefB7FEslDI6ul1eK0ZpmFn2VEL63hSuV4Y+AmJsk+U5eGDcJKKo7\nKSc25CG6rcnMKgfqro31R+/EuaJDYRz7AK4tCsIIyZGoTdAJBLjLtzLCwfhT8SPC\nDYlr2VM+D4MnXJf4U3/h\n=FOMY\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-22T07:52:17Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NathanNeurotic/SeekDeep-DiscordBot/commit/edbef33d3fa0e46108cab247216bf40c89142a74","node_id":"C_kwDOSly7ZdoAKGVkYmVmMzNkM2ZhMGU0NjEwOGNhYjI0NzIxNmJmNDBjODkxNDJhNzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NathanNeurotic/SeekDeep-DiscordBot/commit/b7c290bd4425100db44b47400eec1540b573de72","sha":"b7c290bd4425100db44b47400eec1540b573de72","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NathanNeurotic/SeekDeep-DiscordBot/commits/b7c290bd4425100db44b47400eec1540b573de72"}],"sha":"edbef33d3fa0e46108cab247216bf40c89142a74","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NathanNeurotic/SeekDeep-DiscordBot/commits/edbef33d3fa0e46108cab247216bf40c89142a74"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/109461996?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NathanNeurotic","id":109461996,"login":"NathanNeurotic","node_id":"U_kgDOBoZB7A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NathanNeurotic","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NathanNeurotic/SeekDeep-DiscordBot/commits/b7c290bd4425100db44b47400eec1540b573de72/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-22T06:52:51Z","email":"noahtkevans@gmail.com","name":"NathanNeurotic (Ripto)"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-22T06:52:51Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(gui): Model Manager — RESIDENT vs PINNED shown as separate facts (v10.38.206) (#248)\n\nThe model-state badge conflated two orthogonal things and painted both the\nsame cyan, so it read as confusing/contradictory:\n\n  RESIDENT = loaded in VRAM right now\n  PINNED   = Keep Resident is on (held across task switches; loads on first use)\n\nA model can be both, but the badge checked \"loaded now\" first and stopped, so a\npinned+loaded chat model showed only RESIDENT while a pinned-but-not-loaded image\nmodel showed PINNED in the same cyan — visually identical to \"in VRAM\".\n\nBadge now reports both dimensions: RESIDENT · PINNED / RESIDENT / PINNED /\nUNLOADED, with PINNED-but-not-loaded in amber (warn) so it is distinct from\nloaded, plus a per-pill hover tooltip. Legend at the top of the page synced to\nmatch (PINNED → amber + tooltips on all four states).\n\nGUI-only; applies on next GUI self-update.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ba5bdac02546d04ca1d0e89fd9c575644925586d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NathanNeurotic/SeekDeep-DiscordBot/git/trees/ba5bdac02546d04ca1d0e89fd9c575644925586d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NathanNeurotic/SeekDeep-DiscordBot/git/commits/b7c290bd4425100db44b47400eec1540b573de72","verification":{"payload":"tree ba5bdac02546d04ca1d0e89fd9c575644925586d\nparent 0cab872e4bad6c40b2d6c7e3530844b9e4ad580d\nauthor NathanNeurotic (Ripto) <noahtkevans@gmail.com> 1782111171 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782111171 -0700\n\nfix(gui): Model Manager — RESIDENT vs PINNED shown as separate facts (v10.38.206) (#248)\n\nThe model-state badge conflated two orthogonal things and painted both the\nsame cyan, so it read as confusing/contradictory:\n\n  RESIDENT = loaded in VRAM right now\n  PINNED   = Keep Resident is on (held across task switches; loads on first use)\n\nA model can be both, but the badge checked \"loaded now\" first and stopped, so a\npinned+loaded chat model showed only RESIDENT while a pinned-but-not-loaded image\nmodel showed PINNED in the same cyan — visually identical to \"in VRAM\".\n\nBadge now reports both dimensions: RESIDENT · PINNED / RESIDENT / PINNED /\nUNLOADED, with PINNED-but-not-loaded in amber (warn) so it is distinct from\nloaded, plus a per-pill hover tooltip. Legend at the top of the page synced to\nmatch (PINNED → amber + tooltips on all four states).\n\nGUI-only; applies on next GUI self-update.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqONvDCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJ2IQAHusD9/15vE9fsLWiS6Lo6CY\n8X7o40pOo0I4Fld+tr4vDvdvAtkPIfznEFEMxhepynIwk1/kPh4I6PnO7V7rJuKS\nrADdmUlfhvWn//0su8pKLaLQKqOuZmDYcQ/VwuwvCOS60gX96uERJqYUwY3Npklu\nMUqqaHN39msaHphgjcVYocb34gffXWMhz292NGlTzmEz6AkS6InNiX3AnBi9W0GP\nAfjC6vF2mMP3kHB4nK+xubE1SI2h21BFOE/Tp8VdaDmN5OgEdnFQXJ4pGxm4rFjW\nVQmKgp/Z9vVjEAOgq1VKdEri12xEmu4Xt6+SEesI5