/api.github.com/users/dadviegas/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dadviegas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dadviegas/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dadviegas","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dadviegas/atlantis-azores/commits/32a62a9e9e0ea489996d465bd15f6a023eaaac1c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-24T16:15:14Z","email":"dadviegas@gmail.com","name":"dadviegas"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-24T16:15:14Z","email":"dadviegas@gmail.com","name":"dadviegas"},"message":"Add comprehensive documentation on frontend infrastructure topics\n\n- Introduced a new document on monorepos, detailing workspace management, task runners, caching strategies, and versioning.\n- Added a section on package managers, comparing npm, yarn, pnpm, and Bun, including their lockfile formats and install algorithms.\n- Created a guide on source maps, explaining their importance, variants, production stripping, and integration with error-tracking services.\n- Documented transpilers, outlining the differences between TypeScript, Babel, SWC, and esbuild, including their use cases and performance.\n- Explained tree-shaking, its requirements, common pitfalls, and how to verify its effectiveness in bundles.\n- Added a section on Vite, detailing its dual role as a dev server and production builder, along with its configuration and gotchas.\n- Introduced a comparison between Webpack and Rspack, highlighting similarities, differences, performance expectations, and migration strategies.","tree":{"sha":"2aa5bd0f55566b9c428055f9fe692721488c98b2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dadviegas/atlantis-azores/git/trees/2aa5bd0f55566b9c428055f9fe692721488c98b2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dadviegas/atlantis-azores/git/commits/32a62a9e9e0ea489996d465bd15f6a023eaaac1c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signatur