mission-control-plus/commit/e4640e3c83128bb9b3d981629cf563c4f8d87a3b","sha":"e4640e3c83128bb9b3d981629cf563c4f8d87a3b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mbergo/mission-control-plus/commits/e4640e3c83128bb9b3d981629cf563c4f8d87a3b"}],"sha":"d7ad94929c51017fc1d8d152886856f38aa7f6bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mbergo/mission-control-plus/commits/d7ad94929c51017fc1d8d152886856f38aa7f6bd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13073663?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imtylervo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imtylervo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imtylervo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imtylervo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/imtylervo","id":13073663,"login":"imtylervo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMDczNjYz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imtylervo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imtylervo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imtylervo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imtylervo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imtylervo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/imtylervo","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mbergo/mission-control-plus/commits/e4640e3c83128bb9b3d981629cf563c4f8d87a3b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-07T04:09:32Z","email":"toanntq@gmail.com","name":"Tyler Vo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-07T04:09:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(gateway-url): downgrade http(s)://localhost inputs to ws:// for the gateway WebSocket (#629)\n\nThe gateway runs on plain HTTP locally; only a reverse proxy that\nexplicitly terminates TLS in front of it speaks wss://. Before this\nchange, buildGatewayWebSocketUrl preserved any user-set protocol on\nlocalhost inputs — including http:// and https://, which are not\nvalid WebSocket schemes. A user passing host=''https://127.0.0.1:18789''\ngot ''https://127.0.0.1:18789'' back verbatim instead of the expected\n''ws://127.0.0.1:18789''.\n\nThis is an additive tightening on top of the reverse-proxy fix in\na020d1b — that change already routes the NEXT_PUBLIC_GATEWAY_REVERSE_PROXY=1\npath to wss:// when the browser is on HTTPS, and that behavior is\npreserved here. The only new constraint is: for localhost, http://\nand https:// (and bare ws://) collapse to ws://; wss:// stays wss://\nas the operator''s explicit TLS-terminator opt-in.\n\nTests:\n\n- New: ''downgrades http://localhost to ws://'' covers the plain HTTP\n  case (http://localhost:18789 → ws://localhost:18789).\n- New: ''preserves explicit wss:// on localhost (reverse-proxy TLS\n  opt-in)'' pins the reverse-proxy contract — wss://127.0.0.1:18789\n  passes through unchanged.\n- Pre-existing ''downgrades https://127.0.0.1 to ws:// when no reverse\n  proxy is configured'' continues to assert the https://localhost path.\n\nAll 17 cases in src/lib/__tests__/gateway-url.test.ts pass; full\nvitest suite and tsc --noEmit are green.","tree":{"sha":"1c167abd059db96ac23bee819624e30f5879cf57","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mbergo/mission-control-plus/git/trees/1c167abd059db96ac23bee819624e30f5879cf57"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mbergo/mission-control-plus/git/commits/e4640e3c83128bb9b3d981629cf563c4f8d87a3b","verification":{"payload":"tree 1c167abd059db96ac23bee819624e30f5879cf57\nparent c29e8a50566c6792696669d7746f14955edc93ca\nauthor Tyler Vo <toanntq@gmail.com> 1778126972 +1000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778126972 +0700\n\nfix(gateway-url): downgrade http(s)://localhost inputs to ws:// for the gateway WebSocket (#629)\n\nThe gateway runs on plain HTTP locally; only a reverse proxy that\nexplicitly terminates TLS in front of it speaks wss://. Before this\nchange, buildGatewayWebSocketUrl preserved any user-set protocol on\nlocalhost inputs — including http:// and https://, which are not\nvalid WebSocket schemes. A user passing host=''https://127.0.0.1:18789''\ngot ''https://127.0.0.1:18789'' back verbatim instead of the expected\n''ws://127.0.0.1:18789''.\n\nThis is an additive tightening on top of the reverse-proxy fix in\na020d1b — that change already routes the NEXT_PUBLIC_GATEWAY_REVERSE_PROXY=1\npath to wss:// when the browser is on HTTPS, and that behavior is\npreserved here. The only new constraint is: for localhost, http://\nand https:// (and bare ws://) collapse to ws://; wss:// stays wss://\nas the operator''s explicit TLS-terminator opt-in.\n\nTests:\n\n- New: ''downgrades http://localhost to ws://'' covers the plain HTTP\n  case (http://localhost:18789 → ws://localhost:18789).\n- New: ''preserves explicit wss:// on localhost (reverse-proxy TLS\n  opt-in)'' pins the reverse-proxy contract — wss://127.0.0.1:18789\n  passes through unchanged.\n- Pre-existing ''downgrades https://127.0.0.1 to ws:// when no reverse\n  proxy is configured'' continues to assert the https://localhost path.\n\nAll 17 cases in src/lib/__tests__/gateway-url.test.ts pass; full\nvitest suite and tsc --noEmit are green.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp/BB8CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWgYQACT4fPHCc+Yl0kuUX3FdLO+y\nQMGj5xQ/Cax/G6T3FvwlqLnNymj3kmOFTQDZBULNUUL/4OWocjhHrc1UvuaD00xL\nNFpV441IhfZCZhGJYe5neA9bzABgfu9SbG/1jqEqnHNKEBLyck1VqJTcpuxJjOSr\ncMxKm4OU0N9CvMDQpBhr7Ni4XKK7N/K/8BSZntb2wSRPyLZqpuYHHXF8bOYN3cvv\nhnZafIvKzfwKULkrhHd770i7hf/EVtGRA6+K+5twGUQ+rHHRUss0uVCxdLLNaFwH\nAdxwAqRc9EXJe7Wt6mWgloLOKZ/GUqTtVgRIyHDIfEaY70+NoFqdd6c557S5LF6o\nQVMcG72TTo5Z/0xnE/uUM2IXuQuEKijEhZ4382IpL+l+8a6WDB+E0ewmTiEE9bh2\nT6W0UxNp99zlGd16a5xtbQ+dB3AzKwu1RUbIPlu2BbmT4nF+6mQXy4ld7OVJxepu\n6B+YcKhT9uiNLCdGsQy2xhxonlne2HrTNBaWLE3Y0/1cn1aZSm07EjJMOdWxyj9H\nSCFznIWZIZ+orioeNYJyrP9BCjybGkeFsWkhJzKvRMtcSask2LIjow/sySa/L9TJ\nfr+KqO0RwaU43OZSG6doR0QTxw4xPKP4RFHGtqp5QrlAhRGjf/Fbu+qmT8OAlTEw\n4oVj5Wfs0BeEVwau7i1b\n=Sowo\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-07T04:09:33Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mbergo/mission-control-plus/commit/e4640e3c83128bb9b3d981629cf563c4f8d87a3b","node_id":"C_kwDOSmOoRdoAKGU0NjQwZTNjODMxMjhiYjliM2Q5ODE2MjljZjU2M2M0ZjhkODdhM2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mbergo/mission-control-plus/commit/c29e8a50566c6792696669d7746f14955edc93ca","sha":"c29e8a50566c6792696669d7746f14955edc93ca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mbergo/mission-control-plus/commits/c29e8a50566c6792696669d7746f14955edc93ca"}],"sha":"e4640e3c83128bb9b3d981629cf563c4f8d87a3b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mbergo/mission-control-plus/commits/e4640e3c83128bb9b3d981629cf563c4f8d87a3b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11814847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kieranhume/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kieranhume/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kieranhume/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kieranhume/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kieranhume","id":11814847,"login":"kieranhume","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExODE0ODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kieranhume/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kieranhume/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kieranhume/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kieranhume/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kieranhume/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kieranhume","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mbergo/mission-control-plus/commits/c29e8a50566c6792696669d7746f14955edc93ca/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-07T04:08:55Z","email":"kieranhume@gmail.com","name":"kieranhume"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-07T04:08:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: persist POST /api/tokens records to token_usage SQLite table (#620)\n\nThe `POST /api/tokens` handler currently writes only to the JSON file\nat `tokensPath`. The corresponding aggregation endpoints\n(`/api/tokens/by-agent`, the dashboard''s per-agent cost widget) read\nfrom the `token_usage` SQLite table instead. As a result, externally\nposted token records (e.g. from custom workers using direct CLI\nintegration via `POST /api/connect`) never reach the by-agent\nbreakdown — the dashboard shows zero usage even when the JSON file\nhas dozens of records.\n\nThis patch makes the POST handler also INSERT into `token_usage`,\nmirroring the columns used by `src/lib/task-dispatch.ts` for tasks\nthat route through MC''s internal dispatcher. The JSON write remains\nthe canonical record (dedupe + cap behaviour unchanged); the DB\nINSERT is wrapped in try/catch so a SQLite failure can''t break a\nsuccessful API request.\n\nRepro on `main` before patch:\n  curl -X POST -H \"X-API-Key: $K\" -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n    -d ''{\"model\":\"qwen3-coder:30b\",\"sessionId\":\"test:abc\",\n         \"inputTokens\":10,\"outputTokens\":5}'' \\\n    /api/tokens\n  # -> {\"success\": true, ...} written to JSON\n  curl /api/tokens/by-agent?days=1\n  # -> {\"agents\": []}  ← empty, even though usage exists\n\nAfter patch:\n  curl /api/tokens/by-agent?days=1\n  # -> {\"agents\": [{\"agent\": \"test\", \"total_tokens\": 15, ...}]}\n\nSchema-aligned with v2.0.1''s actual `token_usage` columns (model,\nsession_id, input_tokens, output_tokens, created_at, workspace_id,\ntask_id, cost_usd, agent_name). No total_tokens / cost columns\nreferenced — those are added in later migrations and absent on\nolder instances.\n\nCo-authored-by: Kieran Hume <11814847+kieranhume@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"fa37b1b322e71dcfb808a87a18cb6e8dd6317539","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mbergo/mission-control-plus/git/trees/fa37b1b322e71dcfb808a87a18cb6e8dd6317539"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mbergo/mission-control-plus/git/commits/c29e8a50566c6792696669d7746f14955edc93ca","verification":{"payload":"tree fa37b1b322e71dcfb808a87a18cb6e8dd6317539\nparent 420e1ff3dfab44e35973577e377fec4b43152c81\nauthor kieranhume <kieranhume@gmail.com> 1778126935 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778126935 +0700\n\nfix: persist POST /api/tokens records to token_usage SQLite table (#620)\n\nThe `POST /api/tokens` handler currently writes only to the JSON file\nat `tokensPath`. The corresponding aggregation endpoints\n(`/api/tokens/by-agent`, the dashboard''s per-agent cost widget) read\nfrom the `token_usage` SQLite table instead. As a result, externally\nposted token records (e.g. from custom workers using direct CLI\nintegration via `POST /api/connect`) never reach the by-agent\nbreakdown — the dashboard shows zero usage even when the JSON file\nhas dozens of records.\n\nThis patch makes the POST handler also INSERT into `token_usage`,\nmirroring the columns used by `src/lib/task-dispatch.ts` for tasks\nthat route through MC''s internal dispatcher. The JSON write remains\nthe canonical record (dedupe + cap behaviour unchanged); the DB\nINSERT is wrapped in try/catch so a SQLite failure can''t break a\nsuccessful API request.\n\nRepro on `main` before patch:\n  curl -X POST -H \"X-API-Key: $K\" -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n    -d ''{\"model\":\"qwen3-coder:30b\",\"sessionId\":\"test:abc\",\n         \"inputTokens\":10,\"outputTokens\":5}'' \\\n    /api/tokens\n  # -> {\"success\": true, ...} written to JSON\n  curl /api/tokens/by-agent?days=1\n  # -> {\"agents\": []}  ← empty, even though usage exists\n\nAfter patch:\n  curl /api/tokens/by-agent?days=1\n  # -> {\"agents\": [{\"agent\": \"test\", \"total_tokens\": 15, ...}]}\n\nSchema-aligned with v2.0.1''s actual `token_usage` columns (model,\nsession_id, input_tokens, output_tokens, created_at, workspace_id,\ntask_id, cost_usd, agent_name). No total_tokens / cost columns\nreferenced — those are added in later migrations and absent on\nolder instances.\n\nCo-authored-by: Kieran Hume <11814847+kieranhume@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp/BBXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAr2wQAKTS45v+JeSgdIP2H36WyE8n\ncftlUsvv+9H0w7NpUL921jYCaJ71hOwhBzfYjNF92vKRfj1y/XKbsN5Giv0bWECk\nLWOvut4iWmot4jGlwq6BTq2I8mvNyJXqzQ4tQjV9F2GMcYmY1r1TWzJp/69e7797\nV65vW1V6SAQ+PmMAzOmIFpo8DqOJfMuIthqWsnVyCckrTo3DCf8JzJYK/OZswEUA\nFOpXn8z0j8R7FxlObCl0GTJzMssw6uoc7I70SSS12eU8VJBRleBvYQFagnTkVZZU\n2HSYXjMNEtNFVw9WA3CQIP0oqBTaZqIihsCxv0H/mwob0EpLbwRrZ17h0/LALF+s\nGONSLg3FxhUEuxhx2awY0zbsHqIBMBDcgIKwBQUMgfTlRjxtaHF1w6o+wtRSI9y3\nIzkOgqQ6oR5mf8iwFkPYOu3SBf46jGrGwvTIC+B/wzWewdYeovfvR392s9CgRQKk\nJgbxamB8SlN6u4/Z191vWXChmQA75OCT6T1HeQky1EQ48xwsmJWivDMPNFPQCgpi\njBht2iKk6Ia0RYICy30qrhqdPCw5fc7eis4cAW2+YS6nu8BFv5PAaQtkPCgYhh80\nL3hEFSCOAQB2k6IuREouipmaXxNntYORka+oK8UQ7tw5B29OxYRGIA7cztJFZ9/M\nJJwNVFZLEjAHCTu9nJFP\n=bGw9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-07T04:08:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mbergo/mission-control-plus/commit/c29e8a50566c6792696669d7746f14955edc93ca","node_id":"C_kwDOSmOoRdoAKGMyOWU4YTUwNTY2YzY3OTI2OTY2NjlkNzc0NmYxNDk1NWVkYzkzY2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mbergo/mission-control-plus/commit/420e1ff3dfab44e35973577e377fec4b43152c81","sha":"420e1ff3dfab44e35973577e377fec4b43152c81","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mbergo/mission-control-plus/commits/420e1ff3dfab44e35973577e377fec4b43152c81"}],"sha":"c29e8a50566c6792696669d7746f14955edc93ca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mbergo/mission-control-plus/commits/c29e8a50566c6792696669d7746f14955edc93ca"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11814847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kieranhume/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kieranhume/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kieranhume/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kieranhume/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kieranhume","id":11814847,"login":"kieranhume","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExODE0ODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kieranhume/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kieranhume/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kieranhume/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kieranhume/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kieranhume/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kieranhume","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mbergo/mission-control-plus/commits/420e1ff3dfab44e35973577e377fec4b43152c81/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-07T04:08:31Z","email":"kieranhume@gmail.com","name":"kieranhume"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-07T04:08:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: exclude .git from output file tracing to fix self-update (#619)\n\nWhen `output: ''standalone''` is enabled, Next.js''s file tracer copies\nthe entire repo `.git/` directory (~14 MB) into `.next/standalone/`,\nbecause `src/app/api/releases/update/route.ts` references the `git`\nbinary via `execFileSync`.\n\nThis makes Git treat `.next/standalone/` as its own working tree.\nWhen the self-update endpoint runs `git status --porcelain` from\n`process.cwd()` (which is `.next/standalone/` under\n`pnpm start:standalone`), Git reports every file the standalone build\ndoes not bundle (most of `src/lib/__tests__/`, etc.) as deleted, so\nthe dirty-tree pre-flight check fails and self-update is permanently\nblocked even on a clean install.\n\nAdding `./.git/**/*` to `outputFileTracingExcludes` keeps `.git` out of\nthe standalone output, which lets the existing `git status` pre-flight\nwalk up to the real repo root and behave correctly.\n\nRepro on v2.0.1 install:\n  pnpm install --frozen-lockfile && pnpm build\n  ls -la .next/standalone/.git    # full git dir copied\n  curl -X POST -H \"X-API-Key: \\$K\" -d ''{\"targetVersion\":\"v9.9.9-fake\"}'' \\\\\n    http://localhost:3000/api/releases/update\n  # -> 409 dirty: src/lib/__tests__/* listed as deleted\n\nAfter the fix:\n  rm -rf .next && pnpm build\n  ls -la .next/standalone/.git    # not present\n  # update endpoint now passes the dirty-tree check on a clean checkout\n\nCo-authored-by: Kieran Hume <11814847+kieranhume@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"2cee6a3303a7e6decb10e0fe7dff63b26fe7d5bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mbergo/mission-control-plus/git/trees/2cee6a3303a7e6decb10e0fe7dff63b26fe7d5bd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mbergo/mission-control-plus/git/commits/420e1ff3dfab44e35973577e377fec4b43152c81","verification":{"payload":"tree 2cee6a3303a7e6decb10e0fe7dff63b26fe7d5bd\nparent a020d1b7d045e0e09616663ffb39963f432a3f4c\nauthor kieranhume <kieranhume@gmail.com> 1778126911 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778126911 +0700\n\nfix: exclude .git from output file tracing to fix self-update (#619)\n\nWhen `output: ''standalone''` is enabled, Next.js''s file tracer copies\nthe entire repo `.git/` directory (~14 MB) into `.next/standalone/`,\nbecause `src/app/api/releases/update/route.ts` references the `git`\nbinary via `execFileSync`.\n\nThis makes Git treat `.next/standalone/` as its own working tree.\nWhen the self-update endpoint runs `git status --porcelain` from\n`process.cwd()` (which is `.next/standalone/` under\n`pnpm start:standalone`), Git reports every file the standalone build\ndoes not bundle (most of `src/lib/__tests__/`, etc.) as deleted, so\nthe dirty-tree pre-flight check fails and self-update is permanently\nblocked even on a clean install.\n\nAdding `./.git/**/*` to `outputFileTracingExcludes` keeps `.git` out of\nthe standalone output, which lets the existing `git status` pre-flight\nwalk up to the real repo root and behave correctly.\n\nRepro on v2.0.1 install:\n  pnpm install --frozen-lockfile && pnpm build\n  ls -la .next/standalone/.git    # full git dir copied\n  curl -X POST -H \"X-API-Key: \\$K\" -d ''{\"targetVersion\":\"v9.9.9-fake\"}'' \\\\\n    http://localhost:3000/api/releases/update\n  # -> 409 dirty: src/lib/__tests__/* listed as deleted\n\nAfter the fix:\n  rm -rf .next && pnpm build\n  ls -la .next/standalone/.git    # not present\n  # update endpoint now passes the dirty-tree check on a clean checkout\n\nCo-authored-by: Kieran Hume <11814847+kieranhume@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp/BA/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAASO8QADpDkh0BPdTsrMPq+FTIvnA+\nlg4+iIZJF7b0FBVr6K33bYbnYUSwgZ4VpxD/AdZArOQ6OawJYkL7iBfSqHtPEIDO\nqvc6u10d4TL3mct20jL1N61tWY1mAdGXYGMMTuBZf2krMx8cWNi9IUz2lejzbJmp\nUjCRqSkQWYns3VmWzkweNDnF5++Tv06SMraNvHs0ASL2r2C7OZQMbAEvZ5ntXewg\nlO455ppcEy03MnOkLDK/QrgcUBgMVYh3b6fby+X1ERBYElY3H0lkcknA9YFozzuF\nr20KKFOiJPZU/LV6zWt7mNRAGSYYNaLDul0tsQEemUAqyMTBKhJi5I1o90CGM86/\n24XEu6JaKPn7+HpAg5e+N8QYuhORrPo/ngkGzu9AikbOvjuwFoqF8FHiUNepD+I5\nPHMBBJBbbuAfkB1cMLV5fq9Y+s2ITfin5KW9zDReyP/1QG3vTUflElE+svx1ZePH\n5qAhZcsXw75G64RH1D7oKgWrU8f+cyxv0ZdG/lx4iEFPZkpIibwqQGC/vdhxDmYr\nICGEevIZCZzUMafYj1p+98MFw50qG9X7jFZO+wXwQGQoAYSjpi9o+PFLxb/Aa/ns\nMTqeTHbQ3CMVKU3tZAOkvl15TJLp0nLqyzC2o2py4Fwn8OPveaLiRMtPUL2CufuD\nxmEtZNBTosabEj8n0Mo0\n=nMRk\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-07T04:08:32Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mbergo/mission-control-plus/commit/420e1ff3dfab44e35973577e377fec4b43152c81","node_id":"C_kwDOSmOoRdoAKDQyMGUxZmYzZGZhYjQ0ZTM1OTczNTc3ZTM3N2ZlYzRiNDMxNTJjODE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mbergo/mission-control-plus/commit/a020d1b7d045e0e09616663ffb39963f432a3f4c","sha":"a020d1b7d045e0e09616663ffb39963f432a3f4c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mbergo/mission-control-plus/commits/a020d1b7d045e0e09616663ffb39963f432a3f4c"}],"sha":"420e1ff3dfab44e35973577e377fec4b43152c81","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mbergo/mission-control-plus/commits/420e1ff3dfab44e35973577e377fec4b43152c81"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/93952610?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/0xNyk","id":93952610,"login":"0xNyk","node_id":"U_kgDOBZmaYg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mbergo/mission-control-plus/commits/a020d1b7d045e0e09616663ffb39963f432a3f4c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-21T07:00:10Z","email":"0xnykcd@googlemail.com","name":"Nyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-21T07:00:49Z","email":"0xnykcd@googlemail.com","name":"Nyk"},"message":"fix: gateway HTTPS/reverse-proxy, .env loading, DELETE pipeline, OpenCode part table\n\n- Fix gateway disconnection when accessing MC via HTTPS URL (closes #603):\n  - buildGatewayWebSocketUrl now respects NEXT_PUBLIC_GATEWAY_REVERSE_PROXY=1\n    to use wss:// for localhost when behind a reverse proxy\n  - Login page auto-selects wss:// preset when served over HTTPS\n  - Added ''wss://gateway:18789'' to login presets for container deployments\n  - Preserves user-explicit wss:// protocol for localhost URLs (reverse proxy)\n\n- Fix .env not loaded by pnpm start/dev (closes #603):\n  - start-standalone.sh now sources .env (consistent with Docker entrypoint)\n  - Added prominent note in .env.example about NEXT_PUBLIC_* build-time baking\n  - Documented NEXT_PUBLIC_GATEWAY_REVERSE_PROXY env var\n\n- Fix DELETE /api/pipelines returning 400 Request body required (closes #604):\n  - DELETE handler now accepts id from query string OR request body\n  - Frontend sends ?id=N, handler previously required JSON body\n\n- Fix OpenCode transcript showing only token counts (closes #593):\n  - readOpenCodeTranscript now queries the part table when available\n    (OpenCode >= 1.4 stores content in part, not message.data)\n  - Falls back to inline message.data.content for older versions\n  - Added test for part-table path with text and tool parts","tree":{"sha":"e3986389c538210079bcacc88c33e58545c3d43f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mbergo/mission-control-plus/git/trees/e3986389c538210079bcacc88c33e58545c3d43f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mbergo/mission-control-plus/git/commits/a020d1b7d045e0e09616663ffb39963f432a3f4c","verification":{"payload":null,"reaso