cjMyMTI5MTE5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/macrulezru/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/macrulezru/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/macrulezru/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/macrulezru/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/macrulezru/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/macrulezru","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/macrulezru/vue-toast-kit/commit/0c2e8a02859a6d17b1791691bdedde068c0a3e75","node_id":"C_kwDOSmjS3doAKDBjMmU4YTAyODU5YTZkMTdiMTc5MTY5MWJkZWRkZTA2OGMwYTNlNzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/macrulezru/vue-toast-kit/commit/135b43eaf6933e21affecc6dbfde835c5498e536","sha":"135b43eaf6933e21affecc6dbfde835c5498e536","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/macrulezru/vue-toast-kit/commits/135b43eaf6933e21affecc6dbfde835c5498e536"}],"sha":"0c2e8a02859a6d17b1791691bdedde068c0a3e75","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/macrulezru/vue-toast-kit/commits/0c2e8a02859a6d17b1791691bdedde068c0a3e75"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32129119?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/macrulezru/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/macrulezru/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/macrulezru/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/macrulezru/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/macrulezru","id":32129119,"login":"macrulezru","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMTI5MTE5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/macrulezru/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/macrulezru/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/macrulezru/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/macrulezru/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/macrulezru/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/macrulezru","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/macrulezru/vue-toast-kit/commits/135b43eaf6933e21affecc6dbfde835c5498e536/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T06:39:18Z","email":"macrulezru@gmail.com","name":"macrulezru"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T06:39:18Z","email":"macrulezru@gmail.com","name":"macrulezru"},"message":"Fix installContext()/globalBuffer sharing one queue across all app instances\n\ninstallContext() (called from VueToastPlugin.install()) always resolved\nthrough getOrCreateGlobalContext() — a module-level singleton cached on\nfirst call. Confirmed with a test: two completely separate Vue apps,\neach doing app.use(VueToastPlugin, { maxVisible: N }) with different\noptions, ended up sharing the exact same ToastContext/ToastQueue object.\nThe second app.use() call''s options were silently ignored entirely, and\na toast added through one app''s context appeared in the other''s queue.\n\nThis is a real correctness bug for:\n- Any SSR Node process handling concurrent requests, each doing its own\n  createApp() + app.use(VueToastPlugin, opts) per request (the standard,\n  documented pattern) — every request after the first would silently\n  reuse the first request''s queue/config, and toasts could leak between\n  unrelated requests/users sharing the same process.\n- Multi Vue-app-instance scenarios in general (micro-frontends, a test\n  suite mounting multiple apps, Storybook, etc).\n\nFixed by having installContext() call createToastContext() (which\nalready existed and already built a fresh, uncached context) instead of\ngetOrCreateGlobalContext(). getOrCreateGlobalContext() itself is\nunchanged and still backs the legitimate singleton use cases — the bare\n`toast` export and useToast()''s fallback when no plugin was installed\nat all (no component tree to inject a per-app context from).\n\nSecond, related fix: the SSR toast buffer (globalBuffer, core/ToastBuffer.ts)\nwas also a bare module-level singleton, imported directly by both\nuseToastContext.ts''s addToast() and ToastContainer.vue''s onMounted flush\nlogic — so even a properly-isolated ToastContext (after the fix above)\nstill funneled its server-buffered toasts through one shared buffer.\nWorse, that buffer is only ever flushed client-side (ToastContainer''s\nonMounted, which Vue never invokes during SSR) — meaning on the server\nit just accumulates forever across every request handled by the process,\nan unbounded memory leak for any SSR app that calls toast.xxx() during\nserver rendering (the buffer''s own reason to exist).\n\nFixed by giving ToastContext its own buffer field:\n- ToastContext (core/types.ts) gained a `buffer: ToastBuffer` field.\n- buildContext() now takes an explicit buffer parameter instead of\n  reaching for the module-level import.\n- createToastContext() (and therefore installContext()) constructs a\n  fresh `new ToastBuffer()` per call — fully isolated, and eligible for\n  garbage collection once its owning context is (no more unbounded\n  server-side growth from a process-wide singleton).\n- getOrCreateGlobalContext() still explicitly passes the shared\n  globalBuffer — correct and intentional for its own singleton use case.\n- ToastContainer.vue''s SSR flush now reads `ctx.buffer` (the resolved\n  context''s own buffer) instead of importing globalBuffer directly.\n\nNew/updated tests (tests/useToastContext.test.ts):\n- \"createToastContext() gives every call its own isolated queue and\n  buffer\" — two contexts, distinct objects, distinct queue/buffer,\n  toasts added to one don''t appear in the other''s buffer.\n- \"two separate app.use(VueToastPlugin, {...}) installs never share a\n  queue\" — end-to-end through two real createApp() instances.\n- Updated the two existing SSR-buffering tests to assert against\n  `ctx.buffer` instead of the now-context-scoped-away `globalBuffer`.\n\nAll four new/updated assertions verified failing against the pre-fix\ncode via `git stash` (keeping the test changes) before restoring the\nfix. Full suite: 107/107 passing. `npx eslint .`: 0 errors (2 pre-existing-\nstyle warnings in the new test file, unrelated to this change). `npx tsc\n--noEmit`: clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"db35872c0f924940274a63a0378e486e4b29650a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/macrulezru/vue-toast-kit/git/trees/db35872c0f924940274a63a0378e486e4b29650a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/macrulezru/vue-toast-kit/git/commits/135b43eaf6933e21affecc6dbfde835c5498e536","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32129119?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/macrulezru/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/macrulezru/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/macrulezru/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/macrulezru/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/macrulezru","id":32129119,"login":"macrulezru","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMTI5MTE5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/macrulezru/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/macrulezru/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/macrulezru/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/macrulezru/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/macrulezru/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/macrulezru","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/macrulezru/vue-toast-kit/commit/135b43eaf6933e21affecc6dbfde835c5498e536","node_id":"C_kwDOSmjS3doAKDEzNWI0M2VhZjY5MzNlMjFhZmZlY2M2ZGJmZGU4MzVjNTQ5OGU1MzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/macrulezru/vue-toast-kit/commit/ac5ea5b9546418b6462f9ccc2c073e33cc36e7f4","sha":"ac5ea5b9546418b6462f9ccc2c073e33cc36e7f4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/macrulezru/vue-toast-kit/commits/ac5ea5b9546418b6462f9ccc2c073e33cc36e7f4"}],"sha":"135b43eaf6933e21affecc6dbfde835c5498e536","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/macrulezru/vue-toast-kit/commits/135b43eaf6933e21affecc6dbfde835c5498e536"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32129119?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/macrulezru/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/macrulezru/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/macrulezru/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/macrulezru/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/macrulezru","id":32129119,"login":"macrulezru","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMTI5MTE5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/macrulezru/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/macrulezru/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/macrulezru/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/macrulezru/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/macrulezru/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/macrulezru","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/macrulezru/vue-toast-kit/commits/ac5ea5b9546418b6462f9ccc2c073e33cc36e7f4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T06:17:09Z","email":"macrulezru@gmail.com","name":"macrulezru"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T06:17:09Z","email":"macrulezru@gmail.com","name":"macrulezru"},"message":"Fix broken published TypeScript types (main entry + Nuxt subpath)\n\nvite.config.ts''s vite-plugin-dts was configured with rollupTypes: true,\nwhose bundled API Extractor analysis engine (TS 5.4.2) is older than\nthis project''s installed TypeScript (5.9.3) — confirmed with a clean\n`rm -rf dist && npm run build`, which printed the exact same \"target\nproject appears to use TypeScript 5.9.3 which is newer than the\nbundled compiler engine\" warning already found (and fixed the same way)\nin three sibling packages this session.\n\nThe build script then ran a second, full-tree `tsc --emitDeclarationOnly`\npass, which overwrote the correctly-bundled dist/vue-toast-kit.d.ts''s\nsibling dist/index.d.ts (package.json''s actual `types`/`exports[\".\"]\n.types` target) with a plain-tsc mirror. Plain tsc can''t process .vue\nSFCs, so dist/index.d.ts kept `export { default as ToastContainer }\nfrom ''./components/ToastContainer.vue''` verbatim — but dist/components/\nnever existed in the build output at all.\n\nVerified end-to-end with a real consumer-style `tsc --noEmit` against\nthe built dist/, both before and after the fix:\n- Pre-fix, with this project''s own tsconfig-recommended `skipLibCheck:\n  true` (the default virtually every real Vue+TS project uses),\n  importing ToastContainer''s props and assigning a completely bogus,\n  nonexistent prop name produced ZERO type errors — all 5 Vue\n  components (ToastContainer/Toast/ToastIcon/ToastProgressBar/\n  ToastActions) silently degraded to untyped `any` props, no crash, no\n  warning, just complete loss of type-checking/autocomplete for every\n  TS consumer.\n- Post-fix, the same bogus prop now produces a real TS2353 error\n  listing every actual valid prop.\n\nA second, independent instance of the same underlying gap: `vue-toast-\nkit/nuxt`''s published types were entirely blank. vite-plugin-dts\nproduces literally no declaration output at all for src/nuxt/module.ts\nor src/nuxt/plugin.ts (regardless of rollupTypes or entry naming —\ntested both), so dist/nuxt/module.d.ts''s `export * from ''./module''`\nredirect pointed at a file that also never existed with real content.\nPre-fix, importing `ModuleOptions` from the built dist/nuxt/module\nfailed outright (TS2305, module has no exported member) — not a silent\ndegradation this time, a hard compile error for any Nuxt user trying\nto type their `nuxt.config.ts`''s `vueToastKit: {...}` options block.\n\nFixes:\n- vite.config.ts: dropped `rollupTypes: true` from the dts() plugin\n  (keeping `insertTypesEntry: true`) — this alone fixes the main entry\n  and ./testing subpath, whose per-file declarations (mirroring src/,\n  including fully-resolved .vue component prop/slot types) are now\n  correctly generated and referenced.\n- vite.config.ts: excluded src/nuxt/** from the dts plugin''s analysis\n  (it was already failing to produce anything for those two files\n  regardless of exclusion — excluding just avoids wasted/confusing\n  no-op analysis work).\n- New tsconfig.nuxt.json: a narrowly-scoped, standalone tsc config\n  (rootDir: ./src so it can trace the real dependency graph, but only\n  emitting for src/nuxt/module.ts + src/nuxt/plugin.ts) — plain tsc\n  handles these two files fine on their own, since their own directly\n  exported surface doesn''t require resolving the .vue components that\n  break the full-tree pass.\n- package.json''s build script: replaced the broken full-tree\n  `tsc --emitDeclarationOnly --declaration --outDir dist` step with\n  `tsc --project tsconfig.nuxt.json` followed by a small copy step\n  (mirrors the same pattern already used by a sibling package''s own\n  Nuxt-subpath build) moving the two real generated files into\n  dist/nuxt/, then cleaning up the scratch output directory.\n\nNo src/ runtime source changed — full test suite (105/105) and eslint\nboth still pass unmodified, confirming this is purely a build/type-\noutput fix.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9597ac0bfe98cc680d2ce283615cf851077596e4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/macrulezru/vue-toast-kit/git/trees/9597ac0bfe98cc680d2ce283615cf851077596e4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/macrulezru/vue-toast-kit/git/commits/ac5ea5b9546418b6462f9ccc2c073e33cc36e7f4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":f