/users/fnyamweya/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fnyamweya/juris-web/commits/6b0414d2a695521b7fb5095aaf8328b45c072d62/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-04T13:20:55Z","email":"omburaafelix@gmail.com","name":"Felix Ombura"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-04T13:20:55Z","email":"omburaafelix@gmail.com","name":"Felix Ombura"},"message":"fix(auth): remove currentTenant check from assertAuthenticated\n\nassertAuthenticated was throwing for platform admins and users without\nan active tenant context — they are legitimately authenticated even when\ncurrentTenant is not set. The function''s only job is TypeScript type\nnarrowing after redirect() has already handled the unauthenticated path;\nit does not need to enforce optional session fields.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9df3fce0197cf353e31da7079eeaa0f5b597e683","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fnyamweya/juris-web/git/trees/9df3fce0197cf353e31da7079eeaa0f5b597e683"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fnyamweya/juris-web/git/commits/6b0414d2a695521b7fb5095aaf8328b45c072d62","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/57399460?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fnyamweya","id":57399460,"login":"fnyamweya","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3Mzk5NDYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/fnyamweya/juris-web/commit/6b0414d2a695521b7fb5095aaf8328b45c072d62","node_id":"C_kwDOSmlHxdoAKDZiMDQxNGQyYTY5NTUyMWI3ZmI1MDk1YWFmODMyOGI0NWMwNzJkNjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/fnyamweya/juris-web/commit/3f3213437821dd25cf57e35f56eb1cddd54fd73b","sha":"3f3213437821dd25cf57e35f56eb1cddd54fd73b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fnyamweya/juris-web/commits/3f3213437821dd25cf57e35f56eb1cddd54fd73b"}],"sha":"6b0414d2a695521b7fb5095aaf8328b45c072d62","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fnyamweya/juris-web/commits/6b0414d2a695521b7fb5095aaf8328b45c072d62"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/57399460?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fnyamweya","id":57399460,"login":"fnyamweya","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3Mzk5NDYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fnyamweya/juris-web/commits/3f3213437821dd25cf57e35f56eb1cddd54fd73b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-04T12:59:46Z","email":"omburaafelix@gmail.com","name":"Felix Ombura"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-04T12:59:46Z","email":"omburaafelix@gmail.com","name":"Felix Ombura"},"message":"feat(i18n,legal,theme): language catalog, legal acceptance gate, DB-backed theme\n\npackages/civis:\n- Add Language, LegalDocument, LegalAcceptance, LegalStatus types to types.ts\n- New languages.ts resource: GET /platform/api/v1/languages\n- Add me.legal namespace: pending(), accept(), history(), status()\n- Wire languages resource into buildClient()\n- Export all new types from index.ts\n\npackages/auth:\n- guards.ts: add assertAuthenticated() type-assertion helper so TypeScript\n  correctly narrows Session → AuthenticatedSession after redirect() calls;\n  fixes exactOptionalPropertyTypes TS2375 error\n- types.ts: AuthenticatedSession now uses Omit to satisfy exactOptionalPropertyTypes\n\npackages/i18n:\n- locales.ts: add localeMetadata map (name, nativeName, direction per locale);\n  getDirection() now returns actual per-locale direction instead of always \"ltr\"\n\napps/console:\n- layout.tsx: read theme from DB preference on authenticated requests (DB is\n  authoritative; cookie is a render cache for unauthenticated / fallback)\n- app/[locale]/layout.tsx: wrap children in LegalGate\n- LegalGate (Server Component): fetches pending docs, shows acceptance flow\n- LegalAcceptanceFlow (Client Component): step-through acceptance UI\n- app/api/legal/accept: route handler for acceptance submissions\n- console-page-shell: remove unused StateAction import\n- tenants/page: fix \"PENDING\" → \"PROVISIONING\" (not in TenantStatus union)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b4eb01e2a1d64ae0db523cdc0d6dd6d460ce944e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fnyamweya/juris-web/git/trees/b4eb01e2a1d64ae0db523cdc0d6dd6d460ce944e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fnyamweya/juris-web/git/commits/3f3213437821dd25cf57e35f56eb1cddd54fd73b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/57399460?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fnyamweya","id":57399460,"login":"fnyamweya","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3Mzk5NDYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/fnyamweya/juris-web/commit/3f3213437821dd25cf57e35f56eb1cddd54fd73b","node_id":"C_kwDOSmlHxdoAKDNmMzIxMzQzNzgyMWRkMjVjZjU3ZTM1ZjU2ZWIxY2RkZDU0ZmQ3M2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/fnyamweya/juris-web/commit/8d6450ef353e23fb6eba8d08fe69d68b86d2e699","sha":"8d6450ef353e23fb6eba8d08fe69d68b86d2e699","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fnyamweya/juris-web/commits/8d6450ef353e23fb6eba8d08fe69d68b86d2e699"}],"sha":"3f3213437821dd25cf57e35f56eb1cddd54fd73b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fnyamweya/juris-web/commits/3f3213437821dd25cf57e35f56eb1cddd54fd73b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/57399460?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fnyamweya","id":57399460,"login":"fnyamweya","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3Mzk5NDYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fnyamweya/juris-web/commits/8d6450ef353e23fb6eba8d08fe69d68b86d2e699/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-03T13:14:03Z","email":"omburaafelix@gmail.com","name":"Felix Ombura"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-03T13:14:03Z","email":"omburaafelix@gmail.com","name":"Felix Ombura"},"message":"fix(settings): import Switch, Select, Label from @repo/ui not @repo/ui/theme\n\n@repo/ui/theme only exports theme-preset utilities (cookies, storage keys,\nThemeScript). The interactive form controls (Switch, Select, SelectTrigger,\nSelectContent, SelectItem, Label, Input) live in form.tsx and are exported\nfrom the main @repo/ui entry point.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e7087b05a46eede234eb018dcf160e1460d8ae6f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fnyamweya/juris-web/git/trees/e7087b05a46eede234eb018dcf160e1460d8ae6f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fnyamweya/juris-web/git/commits/8d6450ef353e23fb6eba8d08fe69d68b86d2e699","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/57399460?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fnyamweya","id":57399460,"login":"fnyamweya","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3Mzk5NDYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/fnyamweya/juris-web/commit/8d6450ef353e23fb6eba8d08fe69d68b86d2e699","node_id":"C_kwDOSmlHxdoAKDhkNjQ1MGVmMzUzZTIzZmI2ZWJhOGQwOGZlNjlkNjhiODZkMmU2OTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/fnyamweya/juris-web/commit/a8eeec00980932f58b95f1211da341f1e198a50b","sha":"a8eeec00980932f58b95f1211da341f1e198a50b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fnyamweya/juris-web/commits/a8eeec00980932f58b95f1211da341f1e198a50b"}],"sha":"8d6450ef353e23fb6eba8d08fe69d68b86d2e699","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fnyamweya/juris-web/commits/8d6450ef353e23fb6eba8d08fe69d68b86d2e699"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/57399460?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fnyamweya","id":57399460,"login":"fnyamweya","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3Mzk5NDYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fnyamweya/juris-web/commits/a8eeec00980932f58b95f1211da341f1e198a50b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-03T13:07:37Z","email":"omburaafelix@gmail.com","name":"Felix Ombura"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-03T13:07:37Z","email":"omburaafelix@gmail.com","name":"Felix Ombura"},"message":"feat(settings): interactive preferences UI with auto-save and live feedback\n\nConverts all settings pages from read-only badge displays to fully\ninteractive, auto-saving forms. Changes save immediately — no Submit\nbutton — with toast feedback on success or failure.\n\n## Architecture\nServer pages fetch current preferences via the civis client, pass the\nresolved values to \"use client\" form components. Form components call\nServer Actions on each change (toggle / select). Server Actions call\nclient.me.preferences.* and revalidatePath so the next render reflects\nthe saved value. Toast feedback (success / error) via sonner.\n\nDestructive actions (revoke session, remove trusted device) use a\ndouble-confirm pattern — tap once to arm, tap again within 4 s to\nexecute — instead of a blocking dialog, keeping the flow smooth.\n\n## actions.ts  (new, \"use server\")\nCentral file for all settings mutations:\n  saveAppearance, saveLocale, saveMfaPreferences\n  saveMarketing, savePrivacy, acceptTerms\n  saveNotifications\n  revokeSession, revokeAllOtherSessions\n  revokeTrustedDevice, renameTrustedDevice\n\n## Preferences page  (appearance-form, locale-form, mfa-form)\n- Appearance: theme (system/light/dark), density, font size, reduce\n  motion, high contrast — all via Select or Switch, auto-save on change\n- Language & Region: language, timezone, date format, number format,\n  currency — curated option lists, Select, auto-save\n- Authentication: preferred MFA method, trusted-device trust period\n  with preset slots (7/14/30/60/90 days) plus a custom-day input\n\n## Security page  (sessions-list, trusted-devices-list)\n- sessions-list: device icon, IP, auth methods (amr), last active,\n  expiry. Per-session Sign-out button. \"Sign out N other sessions\"\n  button with double-confirm. No blocking dialog.\n- trusted-devices-list: inline rename (click Pencil → inline Input,\n  Enter/Escape to confirm/cancel), double-confirm Trash button.\n  Shows days-until-expiry, last-seen date, last IP.\n- Auth policy card: read-only organisation MFA mode, password policy,\n  session timeout, SSO provider count.\n\n## Notifications page  (notifications-form)\nThree sections — all auto-saving via Switch / Select:\n  Delivery channels: email, SMS, push, WhatsApp\n  Digest schedule: frequency (instant/hourly/daily/weekly/off) + UTC hour\n  Categories: security alerts, member events, billing, announcements, custom\n\n## Privacy page  (privacy-form)\n- Communications: product updates, email marketing, research, partner\n  offers — all Switch, auto-save\n- Data & privacy: analytics, crash reporting, performance monitoring,\n  personalisation — Switch, with plain-English descriptions\n- T&C history: green \"accepted\" banner with version + timestamp when\n  accepted; orange warning when not accepted; collapsible history list\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9b85341ad817fcb0ef12518943fd74e12a1a9e35","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fnyamweya/juris-web/git/trees/9b85341ad817fcb0ef12518943fd74e12a1a9e35"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fnyamweya/juris-web/git/commits/a8eeec00980932f58b95f1211da341f1e198a50b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/57399460?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fnyamweya","id":57399460,"login":"fnyamweya","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3Mzk5NDYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/fnyamweya/juris-web/commit/a8eeec00980932f58b95f1211da341f1e198a50b","node_id":"C_kwDOSmlHxdoAKGE4ZWVlYzAwOTgwOTMyZjU4Yjk1ZjEyMTFkYTM0MWYxZTE5OGE1MGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/fnyamweya/juris-web/commit/501b23553a7b4897389a908ce086fffdc9d3f765","sha":"501b23553a7b4897389a908ce086fffdc9d3f765","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fnyamweya/juris-web/commits/501b23553a7b4897389a908ce086fffdc9d3f765"}],"sha":"a8eeec00980932f58b95f1211da341f1e198a50b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fnyamweya/juris-web/commits/a8eeec00980932f58b95f1211da341f1e198a50b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/57399460?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fnyamweya","id":57399460,"login":"fnyamweya","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3Mzk5NDYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fnyamweya/juris-web/commits/501b23553a7b4897389a908ce086fffdc9d3f765/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-03T12:55:42Z","email":"omburaafelix@gmail.com","name":"Felix Ombura"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-03T12:55:42Z","email":"omburaafelix@gmail.com","name":"Felix Ombura"},"message":"feat(preferences): user preferences UI and @repo/civis me resource\n\n## @repo/civis — new me resource\nTyped client for all /platform/api/v1/me/** endpoints:\n\n  client.me.preferences.get()\n  client.me.preferences.update{Appearance,Locale,Marketing,Privacy,Mfa}()\n  client.me.preferences.tenant.get(tenantId)\n  client.me.preferences.tenant.update{Notifications,Localization}()\n  client.me.terms.get() / .accept()\n  client.me.security.sessions.list() / .revoke() / .revokeOthers()\n  client.me.security.trustedDevices.list() / .rename() / .revoke()\n\nNew types exported: UserPreferences, UserTenantPreferences, AppearancePreferences,\nLocalePreferences, MarketingPreferences, PrivacyPreferences, MfaPreferences,\nNotificationPreferences, LocalizationPreferences, TermsStatus, TermsAcceptance,\nActiveSession, TrustedDevice (and all constituent sub-types).\n\n## Settings app — real data wired\n\nsettings/page.tsx\n  Replaced mock index with a permission-filtered card grid linking to\n  Preferences, Security, Notifications, Privacy, Profile, Organisation.\n\nsettings/preferences/page.tsx\n  Appearance (theme, density, font-size, reduce-motion, high-contrast),\n  Language & Region (language, timezone, date format, numbers, currency),\n  Authentication (preferred MFA method, remember-device-days).\n  All sourced from client.me.preferences.get().\n\nsettings/security/page.tsx\n  Authentication policy (MFA mode, password policy, session timeout —\n  tenant-level read-only), active sessions table, trusted devices table,\n  enrolled MFA methods summary. Fetches auth-config, sessions, and\n  trusted-devices in parallel.\n\nsettings/notifications/page.tsx  (new)\n  Delivery channels (email, SMS, push, WhatsApp), digest schedule\n  (frequency + UTC hour), and per-category toggles (security alerts,\n  member events, billing events, system announcements, custom events).\n  Sourced from client.me.preferences.tenant.get(tenantId).\n\nsettings/privacy/page.tsx  (new)\n  Marketing opt-ins (product updates, email marketing, research,\n  partner offers), privacy/telemetry controls (analytics, crash\n  reporting, performance monitoring, personalisation), and a full\n  immutable T&C acceptance history table.\n\nsettings/src/lib/navigation.ts  (new)\n  Shared getSettingsNavItems() / getSettingsBreadcrumb() helpers\n  eliminating the duplicated inline arrays across all settings pages.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"eac37ee3c0d36e7342f0c6085512e40b014ac3f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fnyamweya/juris-web/git/trees/eac37ee3c0d36e7342f0c6085512e40b014ac3f5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fnyamweya/juris-web/git/commits/501b23553a7b4897389a908ce086fffdc9d3f765","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url"