node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3Mzk5NDYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fnyamweya/juris-web/commits/e08a06d00c854ce5c0fa8db98e91721647407ea9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-03T12:53:21Z","email":"omburaafelix@gmail.com","name":"Felix Ombura"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-03T12:53:21Z","email":"omburaafelix@gmail.com","name":"Felix Ombura"},"message":"Harden BFF session refresh handling","tree":{"sha":"bf1d4a41d0c44895ae5ef3dc668f2e509fadf450","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fnyamweya/juris-web/git/trees/bf1d4a41d0c44895ae5ef3dc668f2e509fadf450"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fnyamweya/juris-web/git/commits/e08a06d00c854ce5c0fa8db98e91721647407ea9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/57399460?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fnyamweya","id":57399460,"login":"fnyamweya","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3Mzk5NDYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/fnyamweya/juris-web/commit/e08a06d00c854ce5c0fa8db98e91721647407ea9","node_id":"C_kwDOSmlHxdoAKGUwOGEwNmQwMGM4NTRjZTVjMGZhOGRiOThlOTE3MjE2NDc0MDdlYTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/fnyamweya/juris-web/commit/8ad8d88438495deb2411eb09d7fc96436d058f2a","sha":"8ad8d88438495deb2411eb09d7fc96436d058f2a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fnyamweya/juris-web/commits/8ad8d88438495deb2411eb09d7fc96436d058f2a"}],"sha":"e08a06d00c854ce5c0fa8db98e91721647407ea9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fnyamweya/juris-web/commits/e08a06d00c854ce5c0fa8db98e91721647407ea9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/57399460?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fnyamweya","id":57399460,"login":"fnyamweya","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3Mzk5NDYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fnyamweya/juris-web/commits/8ad8d88438495deb2411eb09d7fc96436d058f2a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-03T09:59:31Z","email":"omburaafelix@gmail.com","name":"Felix Ombura"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-03T09:59:31Z","email":"omburaafelix@gmail.com","name":"Felix Ombura"},"message":"feat(auth): enterprise permission guards, shared middleware factory, DB-driven permissions\n\n## @repo/auth — new shared infrastructure\n\n**packages/auth/src/guards.ts**\nServer-side permission guards for Next.js Server Components and Server Actions:\nrequirePermission, requireAnyPermission, requireAllPermissions, requireAuthenticated.\nAll call getSession() internally and use redirect() on failure. Zero boilerplate\nat the callsite.\n\n**packages/auth/src/next-middleware.ts**\ncreateAuthMiddleware(opts, deps) factory that all 7 protected apps now use.\nBFF-only (legacy encrypted-cookie path removed), rolling cookie TTL renewal,\nsecurity headers on every response including redirects, locale redirect,\ndep-injected so no coupling to @repo/security or @repo/i18n.\n\n**packages/auth/src/bff-session.ts**\nrefreshUserPermissions(userId) — wraps POST /v1/ui/sessions/permissions/refresh\nfor immediate permission revocation after role changes.\n\n**packages/auth/src/session.ts**\npermissions now read from SessionPayload.uiPermissions (resolved by\nUiBffSessionService from ui_module_role_permissions + feature flags).\nRemoved all hardcoded PLATFORM_ROLE_PERMISSIONS / TENANT_ROLE_PERMISSIONS maps.\n\n**packages/auth/src/types.ts**\nSessionPayload gains uiPermissions?: string[].\nCasAccessTokenClaims no longer has ui_permissions (kept in BFF session, not JWT).\n\n## @repo/access-control — server-side guards + re-exports\n\nassertPermission(session, permission) and assertAnyPermission for Server Actions\n(throw instead of redirect). Re-exports requirePermission etc. from @repo/auth\nso apps can import guards from one place.\n\n## App middlewares — 230 lines → 29 lines each (7 apps)\n\nAll protected apps (console, admin, billing, reporting, settings, support,\ncontrol-panel) now use createAuthMiddleware. ~1,400 lines of duplicated\nauth logic removed. Dead legacy cookie refresh path eliminated.\n\n## Pages — requirePermission at every protected surface (31 pages + 2 shells)\n\n- admin (4 pages): requirePermission(\"admin:read\")\n- billing (4 pages): requirePermission(\"billing:read\")\n- reporting (4 pages): requirePermission(\"reporting:read\")\n- settings (5 pages): requirePermission(\"settings:read\")\n- support (4 pages): requirePermission(\"support:read\")\n- control-panel (6 pages): requirePermission(\"control-panel:read/write\")\n- console shell: requirePermission(permission) — defense-in-depth\n- control-panel shell: requirePermission(permission) — defense-in-depth\n- docs: requireAuthenticated() replacing invalid \"docs:read\" PermissionGate\n\nAll PermissionGate page-level wrappers replaced. Data fetching only runs\nafter the permission check passes — unauthorized users get redirected before\nany civis-core API call is made.\n\n## control-panel server actions\n\nrequireControlPanelAccess() replaced by requirePermission() throughout.\nrefreshUserPermissions(userId) wired after member status changes and role\nassignments for immediate propagation to active sessions.\n\n## control-panel/src/lib/access.ts — deleted\n\nAll helpers superseded by the shared guards. No remaining imports.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3345b1c0f220b5bf879cf21b250eb0a117594b66","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fnyamweya/juris-web/git/trees/3345b1c0f220b5bf879cf21b250eb0a117594b66"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fnyamweya/juris-web/git/commits/8ad8d88438495deb2411eb09d7fc96436d058f2a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/57399460?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fnyamweya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fn