ers/raghavapollo7/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raghavapollo7/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raghavapollo7/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raghavapollo7/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/raghavapollo7","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/raghavapollo7/Finsight/commits/14ab4dffd2d20c03d4f7f68f0954903d9f91559f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T01:30:09Z","email":"raghav.rocks453@gmail.com","name":"raghavapollo7"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T01:30:09Z","email":"raghav.rocks453@gmail.com","name":"raghavapollo7"},"message":"fix: make extraction schema compatible with Groq strict structured outputs\n\nGroq (OpenAI strict mode) requires additionalProperties:false on every\nschema object, which the free-form Dict[str, ExtractedMetric] cannot\nsatisfy — /analyze failed with 400 \"invalid JSON schema\".\n\n- Add FinancialAnalysisResultLLM with metrics as List[ExtractedMetricItem]\n  and extra=\"forbid\" so Pydantic emits additionalProperties:false everywhere\n- Convert list -> dict server-side so the frontend contract is unchanged\n- Frontend: parse backend error detail instead of dumping raw JSON in toast\n\n🤖 Generated with Codebuff\nCo-Authored-By: Codebuff <noreply@codebuff.com>","tree":{"sha":"82cb4364cb8b53c440c6c00baf2c0bbb1a86e405","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/raghavapollo7/Finsight/git/trees/82cb4364cb8b53c440c6c00baf2c0bbb1a86e405"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/raghavapollo7/Finsight/git/commits/14ab4dffd2d20c03d4f7f68f0954903d9f91559f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/187610545?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raghavapollo7/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ra